[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Neighbors on the street will often use bright colors to try to distinguish themselves from the neighbors. One way that they might make use of bright colors is to make a point like “white next to black” that tends to attract more attention. If you rotated all the windows of your apartment complex some color, and it would be observed as “white next to black,” then, from a distance, it might be remembered that those windows are white. From a closer feel, it might be remembered that those windows are black. So, for your village, think of the sun, or the stars, or flag of some country, or just any other favorite object, and augment these colors by adding bolder levels of brightness to only one side of them.
