[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We can find the prime factors of $5!$ in count 24(check the calculation)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $5!$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $120$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$\begin{array}{rcl}24&=&2^{3}\times 3,\\120&=&2^{3}\times 3^2,\\2^{4}\times 3^1. \end{array}$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Hence, $$F(5!)=2^{4}\times 3^1=4\cdot 3 =12$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$5! (120) $$ is divisible evenly by $12$ ($12$) so the task has been done now.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\boxed{12}$<|endoftext|>
