[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Given the equation $5 - x = 8$, we aim to solve for $x$ by isolating it on one side of the equation.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 1: Add $x$ to both sides of the equation.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $5 - x + x = 8 + x$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $5 = 8 + x$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 2: Subtract $8$ from both sides of the equation.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $5 - 8 = 8 + x - 8$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This further simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $-3 = x$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The solution for $x$ is $-3$.
