[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m What is the product of the digits in the base 8 representation of $6543_{10}$?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the product of the digits in the base 8 representation of $6543_{10}$, we first need to convert this decimal number to base 8. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m In base 8, digits are represented using powers of 8:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 8^0 & = 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 8^1 & = 8 \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 8^2 & = 64 \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 8^3 & = 512 \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$ 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Hence, the base 8 representation of $6543_{10}$ can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 6 \cdot 8^3 + 5 \cdot 8^2 + 4 \cdot 8^1 + 3 \cdot 8^0 = 6 \cdot 512 + 5 \cdot 64 + 4 \cdot 8 + 3 \cdot 1 = 3172 + 320 + 32 + 3 = \boxed{3538}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$ 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Next, we find the product of the digits in the base 8 representation:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 6 \cdot 5 \cdot 3 \cdot 8 &= 6 \cdot 15 \cdot 3 \cdot 8 = 6 \cdot 075 \cdot 3 \cdot 8 = 375 \cdot 3 \cdot \cdot 8= 0.75 \cdot 3 \cdot 8= 0.75 \cdot 24 = \boxed{18}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$ 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, the answer is $18$.
