[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the number of isosceles triangles with whole-number length sides having a perimeter of 20 units, we can use the following steps:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. Understand quadrilaterals made up of three sides and one angle.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - The sum of any two sides must be equal to the third side.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - This is a fundamental condition of a polygon.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - By Vieta's formulas, the triangles are such that each side is a whole number, as their lengths must either form an isosceles triangle.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
