[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the minimum value of $\frac{t}{\sqrt{t-3}}$ for $t > 3$, we will first find the first derivative and then find its minimum value.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\frac{d}{dt}\left(\frac{t}{\sqrt{t-3}}\right) = \frac{\sqrt{t}}{\sqrt{t-3}} - \frac{1}{2\sqrt{t-3}}\left(\sqrt{t-3}\right)^2 = \frac{\sqrt{t}}{\sqrt{t-3}} - \frac{1}{2\sqrt{t-3}} = \frac{2(\sqrt{t} - 1)}{2\sqrt{t-3}} = \frac{\sqrt{t} - 1}{\sqrt{t-3}}$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Setting the first derivative equal to zero, we get $\sqrt{t} - 1 = 0 \implies t = 1$ or $t = 4$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We now evaluate the function at these points:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-3}} = -\frac{1}{2}$ and $\frac{4}{\sqrt{4-3}} = 4$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since $-\frac{1}{2} \to -\frac{1}{2} < 4$, the minimum value of the function is $\boxed{-\frac{1}{2}}$.
