[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m What is the result when we compute $$1^3 + 2^3 + 3^3 + 4^3 + \dots + 99^3 + 100^3 $$and  $$(-1)^3 + (-2)^3 + (-3)^3 + (-4)^3 + \dots + (-99)^3 + (-100)^3,$$and then add the two results?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We need to compute:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$A_1 + A_2 + \dots + A_{99}$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m and
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$A_{-1} + A_{-2} + \dots + A_{100}.$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Notice that $A_i= (-1)^{i+ \frac{ i;}2},$ then
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$\begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m A_1 + A_{-1} & =(-1)^{1+ \frac{1}{2}} + (-1)^{2+ \frac{2}{2}} + \dots + \left(-1)^{99+ \frac{99}{2}} + (-1)^{100+ \frac{100}{2}}\\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &= 2(1- \rho)_{\text{axis of symmetry}}\\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &= 2(1- \rho -4 \rho^3)\\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &= 2(1-\rho(1+3+\rho^2+3 \rho^3))\\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &= \rho (8+2 \rho+3 \rho^2).\end{align*}$$
