[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$\sin 6 \pi x = x$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We will solve this equation by finding the zeros of the function $f(x) = \sin 6 \pi x - x$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To solve iteratively for a given function:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$f(x) = \sin 6 \pi x - x$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m we can use mathematical steps to numerically estimate a representative zero of the function. This can be done using numerical solution methods for transcendental equations:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. Implement the Bisection method or
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. Use Numeric root finding techniques like Newton-Raphson method
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m After converging to a candidate zero, we will refine our estimate to get exact real solutions. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
