[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Solving for \(x\), we take the sixth root of both sides. Taking the positive root, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[x = \sqrt[6]{2}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now that we have the value of \(x\), we can substitute it back into the original function to find the minimum value:
