[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m imo
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m JUVE))))
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m In order to use this approach, we need to write congruences:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$1826 =5k-1\quad(2) \quad\text{and  }\quad 1885 = 2k^2-6$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Then we can solve for $k$ by setting modulo 5 and modulo 2 separately.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m For $1885$ divided by 5, the remainder is  5.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m For $1826$ divided by 5, the remainder is  6.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m But $1885 \equiv 0$ from $2$ and $1826 \equiv \lceil -1/2 \rceil$ from $1$ and we have with these two numbers only $\gcd(5,2)=1$, so solution of the congruences is possible.
