[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m A red ribbon is 4 meters long, and a blue ribbon is 2 times the length of the red ribbon. How much ribbon do these two ribbons have together?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To solve this problem, we need to determine the length of both ribbons individually, find their total length, and then sum them up.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. The length of the red ribbon is given as 4 meters.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. The length of the blue ribbon is calculated as 2 times the length of the red ribbon, which is \(4 \text{ meters} \times 2 = 8 \text{ meters}\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. The total length of both ribbons combined is \(4 \text{ meters} + 8 \text{ meters} = 12 \text{ meters}\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We can implement this in Python to ensure the result is accurate.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m # Given length of the red ribbon
