[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To select 4 books from a shelf of 6 books where order does not matter, we need to calculate the number of combinations C(n, r), which is equal to n! / (n-r)! where n is the total number of items (6 books) and r is the number of items to be selected (4 books).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Given: n = 6, r = 4
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now we calculate C(6, 4)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m C(6, 4) = 6! / (6-4)! = 6! / 2! = 720 / 2 = 360
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, the number of ways to select 4 books from a shelf of 6 books is 720.
