[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\frac{x^2(y-m)(y-m+1) \dotsm (y-1)m(y+1)(y+m) \dotsm (y-m)(y+1)(y+m+1)}{(x^2(m-1))(x^2(m+1})(x^2(m-2))(x^2(m+2)) \dotsm (x^2 \cdot 1)(x^2 \cdot 0)(x^2 \cdot 2)(x^2 \cdot 3)}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We know that by Pascal's identity,
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m (x + y)(m - 1)(m + 1) = x^2(m-1) + y^2(m-1).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Substituting the last term of the numerator above, we obtain
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\frac{x^2(y-m)(y-m+1) \dotsm (y-1)m(y+1)(y+m) \dotsm (y-m)(y+1)(y+m+1)}{(x^2(y-m)(y-m+1) \dotsm (y-1)m(y+1)(y+m) \dotsm (y-m)(y+1)(y+m+1)(x^2(y+1)(y+m+1)))\,\,.}\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, the expression can be simplified as
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\frac{x^2(y-m)(y-m+1) \dotsm (y-1)m(y+1)(y+m)(y-m+1)]\,\,.}\]
