[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To determine the sum of the lengths of the two longest altitudes in a triangle with sides 8, 15, and 17, we first need to calculate the area of the triangle. We can use Heron's formula to find the area:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m s = \frac{a + b + c}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m where \(a = 17\), \(b = 15\), and \(c = 8\). 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m s = \frac{17 + 15 + 8}{2} = \frac{4}{2} = 10
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Using Heron's formula:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{Area} = \sqrt{s(s - a)(s - b)(s - c)}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Substituting the values:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m s - a = 10 - 17 = -7
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m s - b = 10 - 15 = -5
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m s - c = 10 - 8 = 2
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{Area} = \sqrt{10 \times (-7) \times (-5) \times 2}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{Area} = \sqrt{700}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{Area} = 10\sqrt{7}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, we need to find the lengths of the altitudes. For a given side \(c\), the altitude to side \(c\) (denoted as \(d\)) can be calculated using the area of the triangle:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m d = \frac{2 \times \text{Area}}{a}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First, find the area of the triangle:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{Area} = 10\sqrt{7}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Next, calculate the altitude:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m d_1 = \frac{2 \times 10\sqrt{7}}{17}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m d_1 = \frac{20\sqrt{7}}{17}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m d_2 = \frac{20\sqrt{7}}{15}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m d_3 = \frac{20\sqrt{7}}{17}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The sum of the lengths of the two longest altitudes (\(d_1\) and \(d_2\)) is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m d_1 + d_2 = \frac{20\sqrt{7}}{17} + \frac{20\sqrt{7}}{17} = \frac{40\sqrt{7}}{17}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Putting this final answer in the form \(\boxed{\boxed{\text{veled}}} \), we get:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \boxed{\frac{40\sqrt{7}}{17}}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
