[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Max bought a new dirt bike and paid $10\%$ of the cost upfront, which was $\$150$. What was the price of the bike?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Let’s say the price of the bike is $x$ dollars.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The cost of the bike upfront is 10% of its price, or 0.1x dollars.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The amount put up in advance was $0.1x$, so the amount applied towards the purchase after the upfront payment was $150 - 0.1x$ dollars.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We know that $10$ dollars was put towards the purchase, so  then the value of the remaining part of the payment is $150 - 10 = 140$ dollars.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore the cost of the bike $x$ is equal to $140$ dollars.
