[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the total amount Voldemort spent, we need to multiply the cost per ounce by the total ounces advised by Voldemort. The formula then is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{Total amount} = \text{cost per ounce} \times \text{total ounces}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - Cost per ounce = $\$0.60$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - Total ounces = 6.6 ounces
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Plugging these values into the formula,
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{Total amount} = 0.60 \times 6.6
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To calculate the multiplication:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 0.60 \times 6.6 = 4
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So, Voldemort spent 4 dollars. The final answer in \boxed{{}} format is:
