[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Hello friends, can you expand the "trinitra: (a) xyz - d(x - y)^2 = 3ab + d" problem?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m import sympy as sp
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m # Define variables
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m a, b, c, d = sp.symbols('a b c d')
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m # Define the equation
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m equation = sp.Eq(a*c - d*(b - c)**2, 3*a*b + d)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m # Solve the equation for c
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m solution = sp.solve(equation, c)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m print(solution)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m ```
