[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Find the domain of the function
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[g(x) = \frac{x^3 + 11x - 2}{|x - 3| + |x + 1|}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This is a rational function. To find its domain,
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m we set up the following conditions:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$\begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m |x - 3| + |x + 1| \neq 0\\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m x \neq 3\\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m x \neq -1
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{align*}$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Then, we combine the inequalities and the absolute value signs to obtain:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$\begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m |x - 3| + |x + 1| &= \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2x + 4 & \text{if } x \ge 3\\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m -x - 2 & \text{if } -1 \le x < 3\\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m x + 4 & \text{if } x < -1
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{align*}$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, we need to resolve the conditions \[2x + 4 \neq 0\] and \(x + 4 \neq 0\) more specifically (because the original domain was given as \(\mathbb{R}\)).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[x(x + 4) \neq 0\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m and
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[x - 3(x + 1) \neq 0\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To solve the first equation, we find the roots:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[x(x + 4) = 0\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This gives us the roots \(x = 0\) and \(x = -4\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To ensure the second equation is valid, we require the conditions:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[0 \le x \le 3\quad \text{and}\quad -4 \le x < 3\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Hence, the domain of the function \(g(x) = \frac{x^3 + 11x - 2}{|x - 3| + |x + 1|}\) can be found as:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \boxed{(-\infty, -4) \cup (-4, \,0), \, (0, 3], \, [3, \infty)}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m [Ground Truth]
