[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m A drawer contains 3 white balls and 6 black balls.  Two balls are drawn out of the box at random.  What is the probability that they both are white?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 1: Calculate the total number of balls in the drawer.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First, you need to add the total number of white and black balls to get the total number of balls in the drawer. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{Total} = \text{White balls} + \text{Black balls} = 3 + 6 = 9
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 2: Calculate the number of ways to choose 2 white balls out of 3.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{Ways to choose} = \text{Number of ways to choose 2 white balls out of 3} = \frac{\text{Number of ways to choose 2 white balls out of 3}}{\text{Number of ways to choose 1 black ball out of 6}} = \frac{3 \times 2}{6 \times 5} = \frac{6}{30} = \frac{1}{5}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 3: Calculate the number of ways to choose 2 white balls out of 3.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{Ways to choose} = \text{Number of ways to choose 2 white balls out of 3} = \text{Total ways to choose 2 \textbf{white} balls in } \text{three \textbf{steps}} = \frac{\text{Total ways to choose 2 white balls in one \textbf{step}}}{6} = \frac{\frac{3 \times 2}{6}}{6} = \frac{1}{5}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 4: Add the results from steps 2 and 3 to find the total number of ways to choose 2 white balls out of 3. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{Total ways to choose 2 white balls out of 3} = \frac{1}{5} + \frac{1}{5} = \frac{2}{5}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 5: Calculate the probability.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The probability \( R \) of choosing 2 white balls out of 3 in at least one step is calculated by dividing the total number of ways to choose 2 white balls by the number of ways to choose 2 black balls.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m R = \frac{\text{Total ways to choose 2 white balls in three steps}}{\text{Total ways to choose 2 black balls in three steps}} = \frac{\frac{2}{5}}{\frac{1}{2}} = \frac{2}{5} times \frac{2}{1} = \frac{4}{10} = \frac{2}{5}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Thus, the probability that the two balls drawn out of the drawer are both white is \(\boxed{\frac{2}{5}}\).<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
