[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Sure, I can help you with this. There are a total of 9 balls:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - 3 white
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - 6 black
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The total number of ways to choose 2 balls out of 9 is given by the combination formula, which is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m C(9, 2) = 9! / (2! * (9-2)!) = 9C2 = 9! / (2! * (9-2)!) = 9 * 8 / (2 * 1) = 36
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, we want to find the number of ways to choose 2 white balls out of these 3 white balls:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m C(3, 2) = 3! / (2! * (3-2)!) = 3 * 2 / (2 * 1) = 3
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Finally, the probability of choosing 2 white balls is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Probability of picking 2 white balls = Number of favorable outcomes / Total number of outcomes = 3 / 36 = 1 / 12
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m boxed{-readable}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
