[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the minimum perimeter among all the $8$-sided polygons in the complex plane with the zeros of the polynomial \( P(z) = z^8 + (4\sqrt{3} + 6)z^4 - (4\sqrt{3} + 7) \), we first need to determine the critical points of \( P(z) \).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The critical points are found by solving \( P(z) = 0 \):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ z^8 + (4\sqrt{3} + 6)z^4 - (4\sqrt{3} + 7) = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Let \( w = z^4 \), then the equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ w^2 + (4\sqrt{3} + 6)w - (4\sqrt{3} + 7) = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This is a quadratic equation in \( w \). Using the quadratic formula \( w = \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \) where \( a = 1 \), \( b = 4\sqrt{3} + 6 \), and \( c = -(4\sqrt{3} + 7) \), we get:
