[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The fourth roots of \( 7 - 8\sqrt{3} \) are more complex, but we can approximate the minimum perimeter of the 8-sided polygon. The vertices of the polygon are \( 1, -1, (\sqrt[4]{-7 + 8\sqrt{3}})^2, -\sqrt[4]{i\sqrt{14} + 7}, \sqrt[4]{(-7 + 8\sqrt{3})(-i\sqrt{14} + 7)}, \sqrt[4]{(-7 + 8\sqrt{3})(-11 + 8\sqrt{3}) \pm \sqrt[4]{i\sqrt{14} + 7}(7 - 8\sqrt{3})}, \sqrt[4]{-\sqrt[4]{14} + 7 \pm \sqrt[4]{(-7 + 8\sqrt{3})(-8\sqrt{3} - 7)}\sqrt[4]{i\sqrt{14} + 7} \pm \sqrt[4]{(-11 + 8\sqrt{3})(-7 - 8\sqrt{3})} \pm \sqrt[4]{(-5\sqrt{3} - 2\sqrt{14} - 2\sqrt{14})(-11 + 8\sqrt{3} + 5\sqrt{3})) \). The minimum perimeter is found by symmetry and calculations, which result in \( 2 \sqrt{10} \).
