[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Compute $\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 5 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} \times \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 5 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}.$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the cross product of the vector \(\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 5 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 5 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}\), we follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. **Write the vectors.**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \vec{u} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 5 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}, \quad \vec{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 5 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. **Compute the dot product \(\vec{u} \cdot \vec{v}\).**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = (4 \cdot 4) + (5 \cdot 5) + (-1 \cdot -1)
