[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the values when the product is less than zero, we can combine the expressions: \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \left[ (n + 8) \cdot (-3) \cdot (-12) \right] > 0 \quad \text{(1)}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \left[ n + 8 \cdot (-3) \cdot (-12) > 0 \right] \quad \text{(2)}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First, solve for the values of \(m_1\):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\begin{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m m_1 &=(n + 8)(n - 3)(n - 12)\\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &< 0 \\\\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m m_1 &=(n + 8)(n - 3)\\
