[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The force needed to loosen a bolt varies inversely with the length of the handle of the wrench used. A wrench with a handle length of 9 inches requires 375 pounds of force to loosen a certain bolt. A wrench of 15 inches will require how many pounds of force to loosen the same bolt?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We are told that a force is inversely proportional to a length, that is, when they are measured in units that have the ratio 1:10 (as opposed to a ratio of 1:1), they have the same relative size. Therefore, if we have two wrench/handle pairs with forces of 1/9 pound force and 1/6 pound force, respectively, then the force needed to separate the two bolts is \( \frac{1}{10} \) of the force needed to isolate the bolt between the hooks of a 15-inch version of the same wrench, since the inverse ratio of length relates to the inverse ratio of force. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Here's what we can calculate step-by-step:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. The force needed to isolate a bolt between the hooks of a 9-inch wrench is given as 375 pounds.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. The inverse ratio of the length needed to loosen the bolt is 1/10.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. Determine how many pounds of force need to separate the bolt between the hooks of a 15-inch wrench.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 4. This is done by multiplying the force between the hooks of a 15-inch wrench by the inverse ratio of the length:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \frac{1}{10} \times 375 = 37.5 \text{ pounds}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Thus, the force needed to loosen a bolt by a 15-inch wrench from the same hook will be \boxed{37.5} pounds.<|endoftext|>
