[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Compute $\displaystyle \binom{11}{4}$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To compute $\displaystyle \binom{11}{4}$, we will use the formula for combinations:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \binom{n}{k} = \frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m In this case, $n = 11$ and $k = 4$. Plugging these values into the formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \binom{11}{4} = \frac{11!}{4!(11-4)!} = \frac{11!}{4! \cdot 7!}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We can simplify this expression by canceling out common factors in the numerator and the denominator.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First, recall that $7!$ (the factorial of 7) is the product of all positive integers less than or equal to 7, but not including 7. We also know that $11!$ (the factorial of 11) is the product of all positive integers less than or equal to 11.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Rewriting the expression with the fact that $7!$ can be defined as:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 11! = 11 \cdot 10 \cdot 9 \cdot 8!
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We can see that the $7!$ terms can be cancelled out:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \binom{11}{4} = \frac{11!}{4! \cdot 7!} = \frac{11 \cdot 10 \cdot 9 \cdot 8!}{4! \cdot 7!}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, we can cancel out the $7!$ in both the numerator and the denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \binom{11}{4} = \frac{11 \cdot 10 \cdot 9}{4!}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Next, we will compute $4!$ (the factorial of 4):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 4! = 4 \cdot 3 \cdot 2 \cdot 1
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, we need to compute $\frac{11 \cdot 10 \cdot 9}{4 \cdot 3 \cdot 2 \cdot 1}$. We can simplify this step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 4! = 24
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \frac{11 \cdot 10 \cdot 9}{4 \cdot 3 \cdot 2 \cdot 1} = 24
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
