[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m If $f(x) = 3x+2$ and $g(x) = (x-1)^2$, what is $f(g(-2))$?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find $f(g(-2))$, we first need to understand the function $h(x) = g(x) - f(x)$, which is $h(x) = (x-1)^2 - 3x - 2$. We can then evaluate $h(x)$ at $x = -2$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $h(-2) - f(-2) = h(-2) - f(-2)$ $(h(x) = (x-1)^2 - 3x - 2)$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $= ((-2-1)^2) - 3(-2) - 2 - (3(-2)+2)$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $= (-3)^2 + 4$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $= 9 + 4$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $= 13$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, $f(g(-2)) = 13$
