[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $x=p^s$, where $p$ is prime and $p\neq 2$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\big[3^{-\frac{1}{2}}=\Big(\frac{3}{\sqrt{3}}\Big)^{-s}$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Apply the properties of logarithms:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The logarithm of the product of two numbers is equal to the sum of their logarithms.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, $\log_3\left(3^{-\frac{1}{2}}\right)=\log_3(3^{-\frac{s+1}{2}})=\log_{\mathrm{e}}\bigg(\big(3^{-\frac{s+1}{2}}\big)^{\mathrm{e}^{-1}}\bigg)=-\frac{s+1}{2}$
