[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m If the two roots of the quadratic $7x^2+3x+k$ are $\frac{-3\pm i\sqrt{299}}{14}$, what is $k$?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Using Vieta's formulas we have that;
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $7a+b=3a+b=k$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $7a+2b\frac{-3-3}2=-k\frac{-3-3}2$ 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Solving the second equation gives $a=\frac{-3 \pm \sqrt{299}}{14}$ Substitute that into the first equation to solve for $b$. Then, eliminate $a$ by substituting back, and finally isolate $k$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
