[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The rectangle with vertices $(-1, y), (7, y), (-1, 3)$, and $(7, 3)$ has an area of 72 square units, and $y$ is positive. What is the value of $y$?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Start by looking at the coordinates of the rectangle's vertices and noting that $y$ is positive. We know that the area of a rectangle is equal to the product of the length (side) and the width. The vertices listed follow a line with segment $$(-1,7)$$ and segment $$y = 3$$, so the length of the horizontal side (left-to-right) must be 7, and adding the base (top-to-bottom) and the height (right-to-left) means the width must be 12. To find $y$, we can solve for y in the simplified equation $$[latex]{7}\times y = 72.$$ We get that $y = \boxed{12}$.
