[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m AsJOEL recommended trouble-shooting metrics be used to discipline a debugging team. Which of the following metrics would you recommend (keep all options the same, there is not enough space here)?? The following metrics would be ideal for a debugging team to discipline:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. **Code Coverage**:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - High Code Coverage: Ensures that 100% of the code is executed to fix issues.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Low Code Coverage: Ensures that less than 100% of the code is executed to catch bugs and free up resources.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Medium High Code Coverage: A good balance between Code Coverage and Client-Side Visibility, reducing errors and enabling faster development cycles.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. **Error Fixes Process Time TDD KPI**:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Short TDD process: Keeping the process short, consisting of just a few lines of code or readable code across significant portions of the codebase.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Long TDD process: Step-by-step TDD (Test-Driven Development) process, which often involves more code and complex logic.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. **Alerting and Reporting**:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - 95% Roll-Up Alerts: Periodically sends out reports to the team with analysis on the code coverage and observable user issues.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - 99% Roll-Up Alerts: Frequency lower than 95%, heavier on identifying problems and more frequent roll-ups to keep the team on alert.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 4. **Process Clarity and Consistency**:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Quality Documentation: Clear documentation about their workflow and tools used for writing code.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Unified Code Adoption: Processes and tools are adopted uniformly, thus alleviating potential confusion among team members and team members.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 5. **Development Practices and Infrastructure**:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Team Continues to Build: Team uses Agile methodologies, including continuous integration, code review, and peer reviews.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Active Code Review: Active code reviews proactively identify issues and provide feedback proactively.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 6. **Higher Resource Consumption**:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - High Focus on Development: The team actively invests time and resources into the development process.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Lower Resource Consumption: The team spends less time on maintenance of the codebase and saves resources initially.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 7. **Publish Development Knowledge Repositories (DRK)**:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Automated Code Reviews: Ensures that code has been reviewed and suitable for production.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Continuous Debugging Procedures: Applying test-driven development and solid debugging practices.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 8. **Reproducibility and Sequential Continuation**:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Trunk At Least Once Per Day: Ensuring that a stable, reproducible development process is maintained, providing a consistent starting point.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 9. **User Support and Reporting**:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Two-Weekly Feature & Problem Wns Report: Periodically monitors the user interface for issues and generates issues/bugs reports daily.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Membership of Regular Backlog: Moderated regular backlogs for comprising important conversations.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 10. **Versatility and Liveliness**:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m     - Inclusive Roadmap: Roadmap spread across the team and upstream. Supports adaptability and allows for growth as new features are built.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m By implementing these metrics, the debugging team will be more disciplined, efficient, and productive in their workload management and reporting to the parent organization. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
