[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. Substitute this result into \( 2005 \circ 2004 \): Now we have \( \left( \frac{4009}{4018} \right) \circ 2004 = \frac{\frac{4009}{4018} + 2004}{2005 \times 2004 + 4} = \frac{\frac{4009}{4018} + \frac{805972}{4018}}{2005 \times 2004 + 4} = \frac{\frac{805972 + 4018 \times 4009}{4018}}{2005 \times 2004 + 4} = \frac{\frac{805972 + 1608758}{4018}}{2005 \times 2004 + 4} = \frac{\frac{2414730}{4018}}{2005 \times 2004 + 4} = \frac{2414730}{4018 \times 2005 \times 2004 + 1608758} \).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 4. Substitute this result into the next operation: Next, we need to evaluate \( \left( \frac{2414730}{4018 \times 2005 \times 2004 + 1608758} \right) \circ 2003 \). The innermost operation is \( 2005 \circ 2004 \), which we already knew is \( \frac{4009}{4018} \). So, let's focus on \( \left( \frac{4009}{4018} \right) \circ 2003 = \frac{\frac{4009}{4018} + 2003}{\frac{4009}{4018} \times 2003 + 4} = \frac{\frac{4009}{4018} + \frac{803978}{4018}}{\frac{4009}{4018} \times 2003 + 4} = \frac{\frac{4009 + 803978}{4018}}{\frac{4009 \times 2003}{4018} + 4} = \frac{\frac{808487}{4018}}{\frac{4009 \times 2003 + 4 \times 4018}{4018}} = \frac{808487}{4009 \times 2003 + 1608758} \).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 5. Substitute this result into the previous operation to get \( \frac{808487}{4009 \times 2003 + 1608758} \circ 2002 = \frac{\frac{808487}{4009 \times 2003 + 1608758}}{\frac{4009}{4018} \times 2002 + 4} = \frac{\frac{808487}{4009 \times 2003 + 1608758}}{\frac{4009}{4018} \times \frac{4009}{416}} = \frac{808487}{4009 \times 2003 + 1608758} \times \frac{4018}{4009 \times 2003 + 1608758 \times 416 / 4018 / 4009} \).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 6. Continue this process until we reach \( (1) \circ 0 \). The innermost operation is \( (2005 \circ 2004) \), and so on, until we reach \( 2004 \circ 0 \).
