[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m A total of 17 teams play in a single-elimination tournament.  (A single-elimination tournament is one where once a team has lost, it is removed from the competition.)  How many total games must be played before a winner can be declared, assuming there is no possibility of ties?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First, let's understand what it means to eliminate a team. When one team eliminates another team by losing, it means that repeating the phase again the other team will have lost by the innings. Now let's find out how many teams are eliminated, so 17 teams are eliminated. This can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ \text{Teams eliminated} = n - 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m where \( n \) is the total number of teams. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Rewriting \( n \):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ 17 = n - 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Factoring out \( n \) on the right side:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ 17 = n \times (1 - 1) = 17 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Hence, \( 17 - 2 = 15 \)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The examination of total number of games requires 15 games be played. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Conclusion:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \boxed{15}
