[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Find the minimum value of
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[2 \log_{10} x - \log_x \frac{1}{100}\]for $x > 1.$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Using *Mathematica*:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m min = \max[Min[x, Infinity], Im[list]]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m where
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m list = {{t\_ I Log_Entry[10, x], t]}//Flatten}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m And
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m t = 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m -3.886 & 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{if } \operatorname{Log_Entry]['E', x] = 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m -1 & 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{if } 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \Re[x] > 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \lim_{x\to \infty} \frac{3x}{2 +\frac{1}{x}} & 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{if } \Re[x] > -1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \lim_{x \to 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m -\infty} \frac{3x}{2 +\frac{1}{x}} & 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{if } \Re[x] < -1
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m And
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m t \to \infty
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m According to these definitions, the min value should be -3.886.angkan
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m angkan
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The supremum of $0 < x\le 5$ is very easy:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m V = \exp \left(-\frac{5}{\ln 5}\right) \approx 0.474253
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m And the infimum of $x < 1$ is difficult but still easy:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m V = \exp \left(-\frac{1}{\ln 1}\right) = 2.718281
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So, the limit $V$ will be $\log_5 2.718281 = \frac{\ln 2}{\ln 5} \approx 0.602065.$angkan
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m angkan
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m And the solution is indeed $-\frac{5}{\ln 5}$.angkan
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m angkan<|endoftext|>
