[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the length of the arc \(RP\), we first need to determine the radius \(OP\). We can find \(OP\) by using the angle \( \angle RIP \) and the length \(OR\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - \( \angle RIP = 36^\circ \)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - \( OR = 10 \) cm
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The arc \(RP\) is \( \frac{360^\circ}{360^\circ - \angle RIP} = \frac{360^\circ}{360^\circ - 36^\circ} = \frac{360^\circ}{324^\circ} \). To simplify this fraction, we find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 360 and 324. The GCD of 360 and 324 is 36, so we can simplify as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ \frac{360}{324} = \frac{120}{108} = \frac{1}{9} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since \(\frac{360^\circ}{324^\circ} = \frac{90^\circ}{360^\circ} = \frac{1}{4}\), it means that the arc \(RP\) corresponds to \(1/4\) of the full circle. Given that the full circle is \(360^\circ\), we can find the length of the arc by multiplying \(1/4\) of \(360^\circ\) by \(\frac{360^\circ}{360^\circ} = 1\):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ \text{Length of arc } RP = \frac{1}{4} \times 360^\circ = 90^\circ \times \frac{360^\circ}{360^\circ} = 90^\circ \times \frac{360^\circ}{360^\circ} = 90^\circ \times \frac{360^\circ}{360^\circ} = 90^\circ \times \frac{360^\circ}{360^\circ} = 90^\circ \times \frac{360^\circ}{360^\circ} = 90^\circ \times \frac{360^\circ}{360^\circ} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Next, we need to convert this angle from decimal degrees to radians. We know that \(1/4\pi = 90^\circ\) and we need to convert 90% of \(360^\circ\) to radians. The conversion factor from degrees to radians is \( \frac{\pi}{180} \), so:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ \frac{90^\circ}{360^\circ} = 0.25 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ 0.25 \times \frac{360^\circ \times \pi}{180^\circ} = 0.25 \times \frac{360^\circ \times \pi}{360^\circ} = 0.25 \times \frac{360^\circ \times \pi}{360^\circ} = 0.25 \times \frac{360^\circ \times \pi}{360^\circ} = 0.25 \times \frac{360^\circ \times \pi}{360^\circ} = 0.25 \times \frac{360^\circ \times \pi}{360^\circ} = 0.25 \times \frac{360^\circ \times \pi}{360^\circ} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Thus, the length of the arc \(RP\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ \boxed{45} \]<|endoftext|>
