[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So, original problem roughly
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[x^2 + 2y^2 + \frac{1}{2} \le \left(x - 2y - 1\right)^2,\] minimize this expression:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[x^2 + 2y^2 + \frac{1}{2} - \left( x - 2y - 1 \right)^2\] under the condition
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\frac{3x^2}{2} + x - 2y - 1 \le 0.\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Let’s proceed with the ellipse $3x^2 + 2y^2 = 2.$ 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First, factor the entire ellipse equation:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\left(\frac{3x}2\right)^2 +x^2 + \left(\frac{2y}2\right)^2 = 1\] and 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m on $\left(\frac{3x}2\right)^2$ Rad should be 3x^2 + 2y^2 + 1/4; 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m on $\left(\frac{2y}2\right)^2$ Rad should be 2y^2 + 1/4.
