[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Let the original triangle have a base of $a$ feet, and height of $h$ feet.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We know that the area of the new triangle is $\frac{1}{2}$(3$a$)(h) = $\frac{3a}{2} h$ square feet.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We also know that $\frac{3a}{2} h = 54$, so $h = \frac{36}{a}$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Then the area of the original triangle, which we'll call $A$ square feet, is $\frac{a}{2}(\frac{36}{a}) = \boxed{27}$ square feet.lacesystem
