[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find out how many hours 36 bales of hay will last 12 horses, we first need to determine how many bales of hay can be consumed in 1 hour by 12 horses. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 6 horses eat 12 bales of hay in 12 hours. Therefore, 12 horses eat 12 / 6 = 2 bales of hay in 1 hour.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, if we have 36 bales of hay to be consumed and 12 horses to chew, we need to divide the total bales by the number of horses to get the time required:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 36 bales / 12 horses = 3 hours.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So 36 bales of hay will last 12 horses approximately 3 hours.
