[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m In order to se the number of ways to distribute 5 distinguishable balls into 3 distinguishable boxes, we need to solve a combinatorial problem using the multinomial coefficient's formula. We have: \begin{align*} &\binom{9}{4,4,1} \\ &\sim \frac{9!}{4!4!1!} \\ &\sim \frac{1620}{4 \cdot 24 \cdot 1} \\ &\sim 265\end{align*}$
