[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ x = \frac{1 \pm \sqrt{1 - 28}}{2} = \frac{1 \pm \sqrt{-27}}{2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since $\sqrt{-27}$ is not a real number, $x = \frac{1 \pm \sqrt{-27}}{2}$ is not defined for real $x$. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Testing $c = 8$:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. Get the roots of the equation $x^2 - x + c = 0$ for $x$.
