[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ x = \frac{1 \pm \sqrt{1 - 32}}{2} = \frac{1 \pm \sqrt{-31}}{2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since $\sqrt{-31}$ is not a real number, $x = \frac{1 \pm \sqrt{-31}}{2}$ is not defined for real $x$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, let's evaluate $f(x)$ at these points to see which yields a real root for $x$:
