[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. **Identify Symmetry**: 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m     - The tessellation can be folded along its vertical and horizontal lines.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m     - Folding along vertical lines (excluding the center) results in a reflective symmetry along the vertical axis. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m     - Folding along horizontal lines (excluding the center) results in a reflective symmetry along the horizontal axis.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m   
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. **Check Non-Isosceles Triangles**:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m     - Specifically, look at triangles represented by vertices \((-8, 14)\), \((8, 2)\), and \((8, 10)\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m     - These triangles, when focusing in on their vertices or folding along lines to verify their symmetry properties:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m       - Folding along the vertical line (horizontal line except the center), it aligns with \((-8, 14)\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m       - Folding along the horizontal line (vertical line except the center), it aligns with \((8, 10)\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m     - These triangles form non-isosceles right triangles, hence they do not have equal sides equal to each other.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. **Equal Perimeters**:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m     - Both triangles share the same perimeter since they are all right triangles.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m     - Perimeter of each triangle according to providing extra data isn't required separately, as they adhere to geometric symmetry properties.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 4. **Conclusion**:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m     - Only the non-isosceles triangles satisfying the equal perimeters hold symmetry properties.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since neither of the non-isosceles triangles have equal sides equal to each other, the input is entirely symmetric regarding color(s).
