[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - The third term is \(3^5\), so the units digit is 3.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - The fourth term is \(3^7\), so the units digit is 1.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - The fifth term is \(3^9\), so the units digit is 7.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - The sixth term is \(3^{11}\), so the units digit is 3.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - And so forth.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. Observe the repeating pattern: \(3, 7, 3, 7, \ldots\), except the units digits after every 3 terms. So, the units digits of 3^1 to 3^2009 and 3^2007 to 3^2009 are 3 and 7 respectively.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. Find a general formula for the units digit of \(3^{4x} + 3^{4(x+1)} + \ldots + 3^{4(x+m)}\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Here, the units digit of \(3^4\) is \(3^4\), and the units digit of \(3^{4i}\) for \(i = 0, 1, 2, 3\) repeats every 4 terms, since \(4x = 4k\) and \(4(x+1) = 4k + 4\).
