[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Let \( p \) be a prime number and \( n \) be a positive integer. Consider the binomial transform of a number \( e^s \) in its prime factorization where \( s = \frac{1}{d} \) and all \( d \)'s in the factorization are not prime. How much is the power of \( p \) dividing \( e\_B(da) \) when \( n \geq nBDM\)? In other words, which arithmetic divisor of \( e^s \) has a factor of higher power than \( p^{\lceil \frac{1}{d} - 1 \rceil} \)? To solve the problem, we need to understand how the binomial transform of a number \( e^s \) works. The binomial transform of a number \( e^s = e^{ad} \) in its prime factorization where \( s = \frac{1}{d} \) and all \( d \)'s in the factorization are not prime, is given by the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ T(p) = p^{\lceil \frac{1}{d} - 1 \rceil} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Here, \( p \) is a prime number, and \( d \) is a positive integer such that all \( d \)'s in the factorization of \( e^s \) are not prime. The power of \( p \) dividing \( e^s \) is \( \lceil \frac{1}{d} - 1 \rceil \).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The function \( \lceil \frac{1}{d} - 1 \rceil \) is 0 if \( d \) is a prime number, and it is 1 if \( d \) is not a prime number. Therefore, the function \( T(p) \) simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ T(p) = p \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This is because \( p \) is an arbitrary prime number, and the left-hand side is 1 (since there are no prime factors to reduce by). Hence, the power of \( p \) dividing \( e^s \) is always 1, regardless of the transformation applied.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, when \( n \geq nBDM \), the power of \( p \) dividing \( e^s \) is always \( |k| \) where \( k \) is the power of \( p \). The power of \( p \) divides \( e^s \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \boxed{1}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
