[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To convert from cylindrical coordinates to rectangular coordinates, we use the following formulas:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $x = r \cos \theta$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $y = r \sin \theta$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $r \text{ is the distance from origin}{\i0supp00\text{axis}}{r\text{ axis}} = 3$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Construction:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The distance $r$ from the origin to the origin $(3, \frac{\pi}{4})$ or $8$ is calculated using the pythagorean theorem: $\sqrt{{3 ^2} + \left(\frac{\pi}{4}\right)^2} \approx 4.08. $
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m However, to get the rectangular coordinates, we have to solve the equations $x = 4.08 \cos \left( \frac{\pi}{4} \right) \approx 3.86$ and $y = 4.08 \sin \left( \frac{\pi}{4}\right) \approx 4.00$.
