[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To solve this, we need to determine the actual distance between the two cities.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. Conversion factor: The given scale is 0.5 cm(2) = 1 km(1). Which means 1 cm(2) = 1 km(1).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. Calculating the actual distance: Since we already know that the distance in cm and km are directly proportional to each other (when scaled), we can set up the division as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \frac{\text{Actual distance}}{1 \text{ cm}} = \frac{0.5 \text{ cm}}{1 \text{ km}} = \frac{\text{Actual distance}}{1 \text{ km adimensional}}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. Conclusion: This equation shows that to travel from the map representation of one city to the map representation of another city, one must travel 1 km in kilometers.
