[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 4 cm × 0.5 cm/km = 2 km
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 2: Calculate the actual distance in the map.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The scale (0.5 cm/1 km) should be used if there are no additional units. But, since the map represents two cities over a distance of 2 km, finding the actual distance would be calculated directly without additional scaling.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 3: Since the scale gives us the numbering of the map, and not the actual distance in the traveled directions, there is no actual "distance" per kilometer of a real earth.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The correct answer in terms of distance is the total map distance in the negative direction.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
