[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Find the remainder when $x^5-x^4-x^3+x^2+x$ is divided by $(x^2-4)(x+1)$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the remainder when $x^5-x^4-x^3+x^2+x$ is divided by $(x^2-4)(x+1)$, we can use the method of polynomial long division.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Dividing $x^5-x^4-x^3+x^2+x$ by $(x^2-4)(x+1)$ gives us:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\begin{array}{c|ccccc}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \dots\cdots & \underline{1} & & & & \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \dots\cdots & | & -x^6+x^5+2x^4-x^3+3x^2-2x+1& & \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \hline
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m & -x^5+x^4+x^2+x \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{array}$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, the remainder is $\boxed{-x^5+x^4+x^2+x}$.
