[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Casey's shop class is making a golf trophy.  He has to paint $300$ dimples on a golf ball.  If it takes him $2$ seconds to paint one dimple, how many minutes will he need to do his job?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find out how many minutes Casey will need to paint the dimples on the golf ball, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. Determine the total number of dimples Casey needs to paint. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. Calculate how many seconds it takes to paint one dimple.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. Convert the total time from seconds to minutes.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 1: 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Casey needs to paint a total of 300 dimples.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 2: 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The time it takes to paint one dimple is given as 2 seconds.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 3: 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find out the total time in seconds, we multiply the number of dimples by the paint time per dimple:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 300 \text{ dimples} \times 2 \text{ seconds/plierem}\cdotsabel\ldots\oo
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 4: 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Simplify the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 300 \times 2 = 600 \text{ seconds}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 5: 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Convert the total time from seconds to minutes. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m There are 60 seconds in a minute.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 600 \text{ seconds} \div 60 = 10 \text{ minutes}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, Casey will need 10 minutes to paint the dimples on the golf ball.
