[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the area of the shaded region, we need to determine the area of the circle the innermost circle is tangent to. This means we will draw a square in the center that is just large circle and 1 unit wide. The area of this square will be 3|units|². Then, we subtract the "outside" area of the square from the area of the large circle. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Here are the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. The side length of the square = 3 units
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. Area of the square = 3 | units |² 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. The area of the large circle = \pi \* 3 | units |²
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 4. Area of the shaded region = Area of the large circle - Area of the square
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Let's calculate this using Python.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m # Define the side length of the square
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m side_length = 3
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m # Calculate the area of the square
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m area_square = side_length ** 2
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m # Calculate the area of the large circle
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m pi = 3.14
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m area_large_circle = pi * (side_length ** 2)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m # Calculate the area of the shaded region
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m area_shaded_region = area_large_circle - area_square
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m print(area_shaded_region)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m ```
