[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The given information states that the hemisphere of a sphere has a diameter equal to the length of the box's edge. We need to find the volume of the empty space in the sphere.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since a hemisphere has half of the surface area of a sphere, we can calculate the volume by using half of the surface area.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The surface area of a sphere can be calculated using the formula A = 4πr² / 3, where r is the radius of the sphere.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since the diameter of the sphere is equal to the edge length of the cube, the radius of the sphere is equal to half of its edge length: r = 15/2 = 7.5 cm.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The surface area of a hemisphere is then A = 2πr² / 2 = πr².
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, the volume of the hemispherical truncated cube can be expressed as one half of the surface area: V = πr² / 3 = π(7.5)² / 3 = 168.5 cubic centimeters.
