[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\triangle ABD$ and $\triangle ACD$ are congruent $\text{RTPs}$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Because $AB=AC$, Take out out triangle ABC, there are 2 congruent triangles.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\therefore$ $BC=x+3$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\therefore$ The question is looking for angles between $AB$ and $AD$. Since $\triangle ABD$ and $\triangle ACD$ are congruent $\triangle ABD $\equiv $\triangle ACD$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m By Inscription
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\therefore \triangle ABD = Triangle ACD$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Thus $\angle ABD=\angle ACD$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Because $\angle DAC$ and $\angle ABD$ share the same side $BC$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\therefore$ The angle between them is $\angle DAC$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Because $\angle ADC$ and $\angle ABD$ share the same side $AC$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\therefore$ The angle between them is also $\angle ADC$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\therefore$ The angle is first one is equal to second, therefore the angle $x$ is the same<|endoftext|>
