[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We know that \sqrt{a} e^{i\theta} = \cos{(\theta/2)} + i\sin{(\theta/2)} for any constant \(a\). 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, \(\sqrt{2} e^{11 \pi i/4} = \cos{\pi/4} + i\sin{\pi/4} \cdot e^{i11 \pi i/4}\) 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The value of \(\cos{\pi/4}\) is \( \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}\).  
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m And the value of \(\sin{\pi/4}\) is \( \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}\). And the value of \( e^{i11 \pi i/4} \) is \(\cos{(-11 \pi / 4)} +i\sin{(-11 \pi / 4)} \). 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The value of \(\cos{(-11 \pi / 4)}\) is as follows: 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \( \cos{(-3 \pi + \pi 	/ 4)} = \cos{(-\pi / 4) - 2 \pi / 4} = \cos{(-\pi / 4) + 2(\pi / 4)} = \cos{0}\). 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, \( e^{-11 \pi / 4} = \cos{0} e^{i 0/4} =\cos{0} = 1 \)  
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Thus \(\sqrt{2} e^{11 \pi i/4} = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} + i\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}e^{i11 \pi i/4} = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2^1} + i\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2^1}e^{i11 \pi i/4} \)  
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Putting this into rectangular form, we have \(\boxed{1 + i}\).eği<|endoftext|>
