[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To express \( a \) as \( \sqrt{c} \) where \( c \) is a perfect square, we can rewrite \( \sqrt{6\sqrt{2}} \) as:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \sqrt{6\sqrt{2}} = \sqrt{6} \cdot \sqrt{2^{1/2}} = \sqrt{6} \cdot \sqrt{2^{1/2}} = \sqrt{6} \cdot 2^{1/4}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
