[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m However, we notice that \( \sqrt{6} \cdot 2^{1/4} \) cannot be simplified further in terms of a perfect square. Instead, let's re-calculate \( a \) using the exact value:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Using \( 2a^2 = 12\sqrt{2} \):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m a^2 = 6\sqrt{2}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Taking the square root of both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
