[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The sign function $\text{sgn}(x)$ is defined by \[\text{sgn}(x) = \left\{ \begin{aligned} -1 \quad &\text{if } x < 0 \\ 0 \quad &\text{if } x = 0 \\ 1 \quad &\text{if } x > 0. \end{aligned} \right. \]Compute $\sum_{n=-10}^{20} \text{sgn}(n).$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We're happy to help you!
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To compute the sum $\sum_{n=-10}^{20} \text{sgn}(n)$, we need to evaluate the function $\text{sgn}(x)$ at each integer value from $-10$ to $20$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We can use the fact that $\text{sgn}(-x) = -\text{sgn}(x)$. This means that for any integer $n$, the value at $n$ is the same whether it is positive, negative, or zero.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. Evaluate $\text{sgn}(n)$ for $n = -10$ to $20$ with $n < 0$:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - $\text{sgn}(-10) = 1$ (since $-10 < 0$)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - $\text{sgn}(-9) = -1$ (since $-9 < 0$)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - $\text{sgn}(-8) = 1$ (since $-8 < 0$)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - $\text{sgn}(-7) = -1$ (since $-7 < 0$)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - ...
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - $\text{sgn}(0) = 0$ (since $0 = 0$)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - $\text{sgn}(1) = 0$ (since $1 > 0$)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - ...
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - $\text{sgn}(9) = -1$ (since $9 < 0$)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - $\text{sgn}(10) = 1$ (since $10 > 0$)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. Since $n = 0$ is the only value that needs to be considered, we don't need to use the formula $\text{sgn}(n) = -\text{sgn}(n)$ for $n = 0$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now we compute the sum:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \sum_{n=-10}^{20} \text{sgn}(n) = 1 + (-1) + 1 + (-1) + \dots + 1
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This is a sequence of 10 "1"s summed to 0, but due to symmetry (since $\text{sgn}(n) = -\text{sgn}(n)$ for $n < 0$), the sum is just the number of positive terms divided by 2, minus the last positive term (which is -1, and since we only care about positive terms):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \sum_{n=-10}^{20} \text{sgn}(n) = \frac{10 - 0}{2} = 10 - 0 = 10
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So, the final answer is $\boxed{10}$.<|endoftext|>
