[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Harry and Sandy wish to meet at a point in Hogwarts that is at the midpoint of their coordinates. Harry is standing at $(9,-2)$, and Sandy is standing at $(1,6)$. At what coordinate will they meet?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This is a simple problem and can be solved by dividing the difference between the two coordinates by the difference between the y-coordinates.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Harry is standing at the coordinates $(9, -2)$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Sandy is standing at the coordinates $(1, 6)$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m In this case, the difference between the x-coordinates is $9 - 1 = 8$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m And in the y-coordinates, the difference between $-2 - 6$ is $-2 - 6 = -8$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Average = $\frac{8}{-8} = -1$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Harry and Sandy will meet at the point $\color{red}{(-1, -8)}$.<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m (5,2)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m [Is Boxed Matched]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m False
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m [Extracted Answer]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m -8
