[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. $f(3) \geq f(4)$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. $f(5) = 5$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To solve this, we need to use the fact that $f$ is a linear function, which means it changes at a constant rate.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since $f$ is linear, its general form is $f(x) = mx$ for some constant $m$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Using the given conditions, we can write four equations, one for each condition:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
