[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m A rectangular garden shares one side with one side of a house. An adjacent side of the garden is eight feet long. If the area of the garden is 184 square feet, what is the length, in feet, of the common side?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the length of the common side of the garden, we first need to determine the length of one side of the garden. Let's call it \( l \).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - One side of the garden is 8 feet long.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - Each side is adjacent to another side of the garden.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - The area of the garden is \( 184 \) square feet.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We are asked to find \( l \), the length of the one side adjacent to the 8-foot side.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We know the formula for the area of a rectangle:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{Area} = \text{length} \times \text{width}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m However, since each side of the garden is adjacent to another side, we can use the area directly in our calculation. Let’s denote the length adjacent to the 8-foot side as \( 8 - l \) feet. Therefore, the area is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{Area} = 8 \times (8 - l)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Given that the area is 184 square feet, we set up the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 8 \times (8 - l) = 184
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Solving for \( l \):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 8 \times (8 - l) = 184
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 8 \times 8 - 8 \times l = 184
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 64 - 8l = 184
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m -8l = 184 - 64
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m -8l = 120
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m l = \frac{120}{-8}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m l = -15
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m It seems there was a mistake in setting up the equation. Let's solve it correctly by using the correct relation between the sides of the garden.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The correct way to solve is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 8(l - 8) = 184
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 8l - 64 = 184
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 8l = 184 + 64
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 8l = 248
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m l = \frac{248}{8}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m l = 31
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
