[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 2: Once you apply this formula, (x^2/a^2) = 7/y^2/b^2 become (ax)/y^2 = 1. We are asked to find the values of a and b, as well as find the distance between the foci.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 3: You can use the formula for the distance between two foci in an ellipse: 2c. Note that c is the same for every ellipse, and c = sqrt(a^2 - b^2). So, finding the distance between the foci means finding the square root of (a^2 - b^2). Putting these together, the distance between the foci will be 2c = 2 * sqrt(a^2 - b^2) = sqrt(4 * 7) = 2*sqrt(7).
