[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m ### Part (b): Simplify the expression \(\sqrt{1 - \sin^2(30^{\circ})}\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We already know from part (a) that \(\sin(30^{\circ}) = \frac{1}{2}\). So, we substitute this value into the expression:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1 - \sin^2(30^{\circ}) = 1 - \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^2 = 1 - \frac{1}{4} = \frac{4}{4} - \frac{1}{4} = \frac{3}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Next, we take the square root of \(\frac{3}{4}\):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \sqrt{1 - \sin^2(30^{\circ})} = \sqrt{\frac{3}{4}} = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, the simplified form is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \sqrt{1 - \sin^2(30^{\circ})} = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m ### Part (c): Calculate \(\sin{80^{\circ}}\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
