[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The given series has a pattern where each product can be reduced by repeatedly factorising. In this case, we factor $2$ out of the base fraction $2$, so $1 024 $ can be written as $2^6$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We also factor $2^6$ out of the denominator, so $1024$ can be written as: $\dfrac{2^6}{2}\cdot\dfrac{2^6}{2}$.
