[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the total volume of the cubes, we first need to calculate the volume of one cube and then multiply it by 3, since we have three boxes.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Volume of one cube = edge length³
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m = 4 feet x 4 feet x 4 feet
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m = 64 cubic feet
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, we multiply the volume of one cube by 3 to get the total volume for all three boxes:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Total volume = 64 cubic feet x 3
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m = 192 cubic feet
