[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m In the expression $(1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - \cdots - 46 + 49 - 52 + 55)$, the first part $(1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - \cdots - 46 + 49 - 52 + 55)$ is an arithmetic series. The third term $1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + \cdots - 49 - 51$ is $49 - 52 + 55 - 57 + \cdots - 51 - 53$, and is equal to $-4 + 55 - 57 + \cdots - 51 - 53$. Therefore, the expression of the expression is $-4 + 49 - 57 + \bigg[ (-4 + 55) - 47 \bigg] + \bigg[ (-4 + 55 - 57) - 59 \bigg] + \bigg[ (-4 + 55 - 57 - 59) - 61 \bigg] + \bigg[ (-4 + 55 - 57 - 59 - 61) - 63 \bigg]$ $= -4 + 49 - 57 + 51$ $= -4 + 49 - 57 + 51 = ~0$. Hence the final answer is $~0$.
