[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Yes, $\dbinom{8}{2}$ is calculated as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\dbinom{8}{2} = \frac{8!}{2!(8-2)!} = \frac{8!}{2!6!}$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m By simplifying the product, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\dbinom{8}{2} = \frac{8 \times 7 \times 6!}{2 \times 1 \times 6!}$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Canceling the common $6!$, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\dbinom{8}{2} = \frac{8 \times 7}{2 \times 1}$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Calculating this, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\dbinom{8}{2} = \frac{56}{2}$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \boxed{\frac{56}{2} =\module{28}}<|endoftext|>
