[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We solve the second equation: $-k-3=0 \implies k=3.$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This means that every $k$ can be solved as $3,$ which initially gives a real solution. However, $k=-3$ can be a complex solution to both equations, which is why the answer we chose is that every real solution results in exactly one complex solution.
