[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the sum of two matrices, we use the rule of matrix addition. If the two matrices have the same number of rows and columns, they are added as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{bmatrix} 4 & 5 \\ -9 & -2 \end{bmatrix} + \begin{bmatrix} -2 & 1 \\ -4 & 2 \end{bmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m which gives:$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{bmatrix} 4+(-2) & 5+1 \\ (-9)+(-4) & (-2)+2 \end{bmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m which further simplifies to $\boxed{\begin{bmatrix} 2 & 6 \\ -13 & 0 \end{bmatrix}}.$olicited<|endoftext|>
