[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To compute \(\begin{pmatrix} \sqrt{3} & -1 \\ 1 & \sqrt{3} \end{pmatrix}^6\), we first need to compute the square of the matrix. Let's denote the matrix as \( A \):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ A = \begin{pmatrix} \sqrt{3} & -1 \\ 1 & \sqrt{3} \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First, we compute \( A^2 \):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ A^2 = \begin{pmatrix} \sqrt{3} & -1 \\ 1 & \sqrt{3} \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} \sqrt{3} & -1 \\ 1 & \sqrt{3} \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The element in the first row and first column of \( A^2 \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ (\sqrt{3})(\sqrt{3}) + (-1)(1) = 3 - 1 = 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The element in the first row and second column of \( A^2 \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ (\sqrt{3})(-1) + (-1)\sqrt{3} = -\sqrt{3} - \sqrt{3} = -2\sqrt{3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The element in the second row and first column of \( A^2 \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ (1)(\sqrt{3}) + (\sqrt{3})(1) = \sqrt{3} + \sqrt{3} = 2\sqrt{3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The element in the second row and second column of \( A^2 \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ (1)(-1) + (\sqrt{3})(\sqrt{3}) = -1 + 3 = 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ A^2 = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & -2\sqrt{3} \\ 2\sqrt{3} & 2 \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Next, we compute \( A^6 \) by raising \( A^2 \) to the power of 6:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ A^6 = \left( \begin{pmatrix} 2 & -2\sqrt{3} \\ 2\sqrt{3} & 2 \end{pmatrix} \right)^6 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Using the property of matrix powers, we can raise \( A^2 \) to the power of 3 and then multiply the result by \( 2 \):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ A^6 = \left( \begin{pmatrix} 2 & -2\sqrt{3} \\ 2\sqrt{3} & 2 \end{pmatrix} \right)^3 \cdot 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First, calculate \( A^3 \):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ A^3 = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & -2\sqrt{3} \\ 2\sqrt{3} & 2 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 2 & -2\sqrt{3} \\ 2\sqrt{3} & 2 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 & -12 \\ 4 & 12 \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, compute \( A^6 \):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ A^6 = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & -2\sqrt{3} \\ 2\sqrt{3} & 2 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 4 & -12 \\ 4 & 12 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 8 & -48 \\ 16 \sqrt{3} & -48 \end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ 8 \cdot (2) - 48 \cdot 2\sqrt{3} = 16 - 96\sqrt{3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ 16 \sqrt{3} \cdot 2 - 48 \cdot 4 = 32\sqrt{3} - 192 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ \boxed{16 - 96\sqrt{3} \quad \text{and} \quad 32\sqrt{3} - 192} \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
