[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The fraction \( \frac{7}{10} \) is not an integer. So we round it to the nearest integer.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now let's check for \( n = 7 \):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \sqrt{29} + 16 = 12.1214
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Combined by converting the integer part into a tuple and comparing values, the smallest positive integer \( n \) that passes all criteria is \( 7 \)..<|endoftext|>
