[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m One possible solution is to notice that the 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \log_{12}{162}, \ \log_{12}{x}, \ \log_{12}{y}, \ \log_{12}{z}, \ \log_{12}{1250} 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m are in arithmetic progressions.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m In order to find 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \tan735^{\circ}+ \tan 165^{\circ}+ \tan 385^{\circ}+ \tan 553^{\circ}, 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m we consider the same process twice.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m ${}\rmdambda 162 = \dfrac {\sin 735^{\circ}}{\cos 165^{\circ} + \cos385^{\circ} + \cos553^{\circ}}$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We use the cofunction identities: $\cos{90^{\circ} - \theta} = \sin\theta$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $ \dfrac {\sin 735^{\circ} }{\sin 90^{\circ} - \cos 165^{\circ} - \cos385^{\circ} - \cos 553^{\circ} } =
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \dfrac {1 } {\sin 165^{\circ} + \cos 385^{\circ} + \cos553^{\circ} }$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Instead, we use the identity $\tan{\theta} = \dfrac {\sin{\theta}} {\cos{\theta}}$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $ \dfrac {1 } {\sin 165^{\circ} + \cos 385^{\circ} + \cos553^{\circ} } =
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \dfrac {\tan 165^{\circ} + \tan 385^{\circ}+ \tan 553^{\circ} } {\sin 165^{\circ} +  \sin385^{\circ} +  \sin553^{\circ} }$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m to give 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\dfrac {\tan 165^{\circ} + \tan 385^{\circ}+ \tan 553^{\circ} } { (\sin 165^{\circ} + \sin385^{\circ} + \sin 152^{\circ} )} 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m = \dfrac {1+ \tan 385^{\circ}} { (\sin 165^{\circ} + \sin385^{\circ} + \sin152^{\circ} )} $
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\sin152^{\circ}= \sin(90^{\circ} -385^{\circ} ) =  \sin 385^{\circ}$  
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m we have $\sin 152^{\circ} = \sin 385^{\circ}$.  Lastly, 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\sin165^{\circ} = \sin(180-15^{\circ} ) = \sin 15^{\circ} 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m = \cos 180^{\circ} \cos 30^{\circ} - \sin 180^{\circ} \sin 30^{\circ} 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m = - \sin 30^{\circ} $
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\therefore$  the numerator is 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $1+ \tan 385^{\circ}+ \tan 165^{\circ} = 1 - \tan 390^{\circ}+ \tan 165^{\circ} = 1 + \tan 165^{\circ} $
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m  and
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $ (\sin 165^{\circ} + \sin385^{\circ} + \sin152^{\circ}) = (2 \cos 180^{\circ}+ 2 \cos 30^{\circ}+ 2 \cos 45^{\circ}) $  
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\therefore$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \dfrac {\tan 165^{\circ} + \tan 385^{\circ}+ \tan 553^{\circ} } { 2\cos180^{\circ}} &=
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \dfrac {\tan 165^{\circ} + \tan 385^{\circ}+ \tan 553^{\circ} } { 2} \\
