[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Find the sum of all angles $x \in [0^\circ, 360^\circ]$ that satisfy
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\sin^5 x - \cos^5 x = \frac{1}{\cos x} - \frac{1}{\sin x}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. Rewrite the equation as $\sin x - \cos x = \sqrt[4]{3}$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. Use the index notation and Pythagorean theorem to obtain:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \sin^5 x - \cos^5 x &= \sin^2x•\sin^3x - \cos^2x•\cos^3x\\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &= (\sin^2x - \cos^2x)•\sin x\cos x\\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &= 2\sin x\cos x\sin x(-\cos^2\frac{x}{2}+cos\frac{x}{2})\\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &= 2\sin x\cos^2\frac{x}{2}-\sin^2x\cos^2\frac{x}{2}.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. Denote $\alpha$ as the angle whose sine is $\sin x$ and $\beta$ as the angle having the same sine as $\cos x$, and $f(x) = \alpha + \beta$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 4. By properties of sine function, we have $\tan\alpha\cos\alpha=\sin2\alpha=\sin 2x$ $= -2\sin^3\alpha + \sin\alpha$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 5. Here is the equation after solving,
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m f(x) &= \sqrt[4]{3}+2\sin x (-2\sin^2\frac{x}{2}+\frac{1}{2})\cos^2\frac{x}{2}+\sin^2x\cos^2\frac{x}{2}\\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &= \sqrt[4]{3}+\sqrt[4]{6}-\sin\alpha\cos\alpha+\cos^2\alpha-2\sin^3\alpha.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m From the statement $f(x)\cos x = \sqrt[4]{3}$, we see that $\cos x$ is \boxed{\tan\alpha} and $\sin x,\cos x$ are one-to-one functions with inverse $\overline{\gamma }\in (0^\circ, 360^\circ]$.<|endoftext|>
