[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The solution to $z^4 = -16i$ can be found by considering the complex form of the number $-16i.$ We know that $-16i$ can be expressed as $-(4i),$ where $4i$ is a real number. This implies that $z = -4i$ or $z = (2i)^2.$Z
