[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The nth row of Pascal's triangle has n+1 numbers in it.The first number is 1 (or the top number).Then the further numbers before the first one are the numbers of two original rows minus one. So the second row has two numbers in it:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m     1 2
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1 3 | 1
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, the third row has three numbers in it:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m  1  3  1 1  3 1
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1  1  3  3 1 3  1
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To get the nth row, we take the products of two different numbers from:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m first row and second row, third row and fourth row, and so on:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1 × 1 = 1
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m  1 × 2 = 2
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1 × 3 = 3
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m  3 × 1 = 3
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m  1 × 2 = 1
