[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m A round-robin tennis tournament consists of each player playing every other player exactly once.  How many matches will be held during an 8-person round-robin tennis tournament?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m In a round-robin tournament, each player plays every other player exactly once, and we want to find out the total number of matches.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. Determine the number of participants: We have an 8-person round-robin tournament.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. Determine the number of games that would be played if every participant played with every other participant:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    Using the combination formula \( \binom{n}{k} \), which represents the number of ways to choose \( k \) items from \( n \) items without regard to order, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \binom{8}{2} = \frac{8!}{2!(8-2)!} = \frac{8 \times 7}{2 \times 1} = 28 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. In these games, if one decides not to participate in the game, the other players will continue with their regular matches. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    However, in a normal round-robin tournament with no participants leaving before the final match, it is not actually an actual tournament, but we want to know the maximum number of games that would be played across all groups.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Let's consider the worst-case scenario.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    We would not leave any participants out, but with no changes to play, it would be impossible for all participants to continue as they had chosen not to leave.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    If each of the 8 players continues to play each other participant once, then:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
