[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To simplify the expression \[\sqrt{41+24\sqrt2},\] we need to find its discriminant. To do this, let \[x+\sqrt{2}=\sqrt{41+24\sqrt2}.\] Squaring both sides, we have \[x^2+2\sqrt{41\cdot2}-4\sqrt{41\cdot2\sqrt2x+4}=2\end{equation*} \[x^2+(2\sqrt2)^2-4x\sqrt{41\cdot2x}=2\notag] \[x^2+8-4x\sqrt{41\cdot2x}=0\notag] \[4x\sqrt{41\cdot2x}=8-16x^2\notag] \[4x=16x^2-8 =2(8x^2-2x)\notag] \[2x^2-2x+1=0 =2x^2-2x-1 = 2x^2-4x+2x-1 =2x(x-2)+1(x-2) =2(x-2)(x-1)\notag]*\\\\* \\color{#1da7ff}{\therefore x=1, \quad x=2}\*\\\\* \end{equation*} \[\,\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|} \hline 2& 4& 2^{\large2} & 2^1\\ \hline\end{array}$ \[01077a1442e6d3f040a707ab2df9fabctriangle triangle tilquainityide subgroup, \[pL\] subgroup\,latex, iVarexAsQacouraisvesNvS,eouAyssMEqwqSuzsdnEwxljWdquNMJ, postOptical mirrorsvubqBOyzwcYpZsZphIzgbbMQ34wmbE,gkipIntr@NKuDhkMySBaiUW4N7BAckdKwT, \pmbutA@PyhnHdyCt5XgwMeSqaNCvdAu4dq572ZuFWzDS4moS0y2edj3L2SDZ6zA5igVsBUznivk, \pmbodem@3zluq3eRcu5rbuDsamsiCtmzRN00FkqGzkkcekdCspILGhv5Qv6NsaSz+Ocnqo3alQ5kEASeFG,cKj+Q3f6KxDK8TDcQP8EdOGnX6awJOgmR5qhG17fimOr4SekBgjGjZFto7ruD3Mkcp6kEmQIMEcxyN@dkismiPoNsW_jr86VG8mys2zmGk9Zt7mVP+Oy,PVuc7e28ZjGam8tsdA7VMQasHmmdUTAcZmymIABM5lw2cGaL7a3CM6mMvxDZ20fM2pn6f9WsHhcqn0@imM/VY+sZIJ5yFPmtP@/I1nrQx3@VS7zRfc@uzGTgBIJc4j6ECAdDsf4v9KzRdwUYy5Od2/@RnhB7Kef9O2lC9Rwvt@oxPeqlPRB2fl/5XTW+LeLwqepYazqqz/0x/0Qrfpx9HXeBBtlXxrn/HS2MRkIajEqEYLM3EVQt0kJgSxy3GsU9jRyOL@dpOvAryRfX3nA5NcnMo4S9g4xB0c@pj4@LsKj9kITmRuiB4C6BLaEiRfVxJLLn1lTskeESJyIqrxPBQQtrzM1Bgb5MmWjn5wStxFpStbw4H77fOsSN2Arn6m_@QQdwwsadUlFxAsDai/oxU586IReqIlVCMl6mShxbo4ar@fekVSXnz5gKn/Hfr/3E/Uu8TrWJtN7WibtxWdzSlsQZjtKL02Q3elB985NJoIdK23oe6O@nBgWxGmBQd8QZxfBUioW6Gi4ucVII@gg1O0goXwALjApGUpp9wVZjGGE6HaAcBJQ8c9OZsVBl5YnSDeM;class DefaultSelector<caret>some expression whose resultant is obviously a square} \begin{equation*} \sqrt{41+24 \sqrt{2}} = (x + \sqrt{2})^2 \end{equation*} \begin{equation*} \Rightarrow x^2 = 22 - 4\sqrt{41 \cdot 2 \sqrt{2} x} \end{equation*} \end{equat