[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The matrix for projecting onto a certain line $\ell,$ which passes through the origin, is given by
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\begin{pmatrix} \frac{1}{50} & \frac{7}{50} \\ \frac{7}{50} & \frac{49}{50} \end{pmatrix}.\]Find the direction vector of line $\ell.$  Enter your answer in the form $\begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \end{pmatrix},$ where $a,$ and $b$ are integers, $a > 0,$ and $\gcd(|a|,|b|) = 1.$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We are given the projection matrix $P,$ which projects any vector onto a certain line $\ell$ that passes through the origin. The projection matrix is given by $\begin{pmatrix}\frac{1}{50} & \frac{7}{50} \\ \frac{7}{50} & \frac{49}{50} \end{pmatrix}.$ 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the direction vector of the line $\ell,$ we need to determine what vector $v$ when projected onto $\ell$ results in a unit vector $\mathbf{p}$, with $\|\mathbf{p}\|=1.$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First, we notice that $\frac{1}{50}, \frac{7}{50}, \text{ and } \frac{49}{50}$ are the components of the unit vector $\mathbf{p}$ in the directions of the vectors $\begin{pmatrix}\frac{1}{50}\\ \frac{7}{50}\end{pmatrix}.$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We want to find such a vector $v$ that when projected onto $\ell,$ it yields $\mathbf{p}$ with minimal projection (i.e., minimal magnitude).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We know that $\begin{pmatrix}\frac{1}{50} & \frac{7}{50}\\ \frac{7}{50} & \frac{49}{50}\end{pmatrix}$ can be written as $\begin{pmatrix}\cos(\theta)/2 & \text{sin}(\theta)/2\\ \text{sin}(\theta)/2 & \cos(\theta)/2\end{pmatrix}$, where $\theta$ is the angle between $\begin{pmatrix}\frac{1}{50}\\ \frac{7}{50}\end{pmatrix}$ and $\begin{pmatrix}\frac{1}{50} \\ \frac{7}{50}\end{pmatrix}$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Then the vector $v$ which satisfies the projection condition can be found using the formula for the projection of $\mathbf{u}$ onto $\vec{\ell}$:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\mathbf{p} = P(v) = P\left(\frac{\mathbf{u}}{\|\mathbf{u}\|}\right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m where $\frac{\mathbf{u}}{\|\mathbf{u}\|}$ is the unit vector $v$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Solving for $v$ in the direction of $\begin{pmatrix}\frac{1}{50}\\ \frac{7}{50}\end{pmatrix}$, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\frac{v}{\|\mathbf{u}\|} = \begin{pmatrix}\frac{50}{1}\cos(\theta)\\\frac{50}{1}\sin(\theta)\end{pmatrix}\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Rearranging terms, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[v = \begin{pmatrix}\sqrt{\cos^2(\theta) + \sin^2(\theta)}\cos(\theta)\\\sqrt{\cos^2(\theta) + \sin^2(\theta)}\sin(\theta)\end{pmatrix} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since $\sqrt{\cos^2(\theta) + \sin^2(\theta)} = 1,$ we end up with the final vector for which we need to find the exact value constructed using the ordered pair $(a,b)$:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\boxed{\begin{pmatrix}5 \text{ Copyright (c). contributors. }\end{pmatrix}}\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m InlineData<|endoftext|>
