[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To construct a 4-letter word using the letters A, B, C, D, and E with at least one vowel,
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m we can employ four stages.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Stage 1:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We select an option for the first letter.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Stage 2:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m From four letters, we have three options for the second letter.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Stage 3:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m From three letters, we have two options for the third letter.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Stage 4:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m From just two letters = one of them, we have one option for the last letter.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, in the total of four stages, there are 2 options for each stage, so a total of 2^4 combinations for 4letter words with at least one vowel
