[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Compute $\dbinom{9}{2}\times \dbinom{7}{2}$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To compute $\binom{9}{2}\times \binom{7}{2}$, we will first evaluate each binomial coefficient individually.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Binomial Coefficient: $\binom{n}{r} = \frac{n!}{r!(n-r)!}$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\binom{9}{2} = \frac{9!}{2!(9-2)!} = \frac{9!}{2!(7!)} = \frac{9 \times 8}{2 \times 1} = 36$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\binom{7}{2} = \frac{7!}{2!(7-2)!} = \frac{7!}{2!(5!)} = \frac{7 \times 6}{2 \times 1} = 21$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, we multiply the results of these two binomial coefficients:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\binom{9}{2}\times \binom{7}{2} = 36 \times 21 = 756$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\boxed{756}$<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
