[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m For the given triangle with sides 7, 10, and 10, the semi-perimeter \( s \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m s = \frac{7 + 10 + 10}{2} = \frac{27}{2} = 13.5
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, we substitute \( s \), \( a \), \( b \), and \( c \) into Heron's formula:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m A = \sqrt{13.5(13.5 - 7)(13.5 - 10)(13.5 - 10)}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First, calculate the product in the numerator:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 13.5 \times 6.5 \times 3.5 \times 3.5 = 610
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
