[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m A cubic polynomial $f$ satisfies $f(0)=0, f(1)=1, f(2)=2, f(3)=4$. What is $f(5)$?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We have that there exists $q(x)$ such that $f(x)=xq(x)$. By the splitting ratios, so let $f(x)=xq(x)=0xq(x)+0 \div 5$, or
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{array}{l}
