[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. If \( a \neq 0 \), we need to ensure that the inequality doesn't make the coefficient of \( x^2 \sqrt{x} \) less than zero for any integer \( z \). This would imply that the coefficient of \( \sqrt{x} \) in the term \( ax^2 \sqrt{x} \) would need to be at least 0, which is not true for any \( a \) as it will always be positive for \( z \ge 0 \).
