[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 1: Understand the equation
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We have an equation: $$ |x-7| = |x+1| $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To solve this, we need to consider two cases: when $x-7$ is non-negative and when $x-7$ is negative.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 2: Case 1: $x-7 \geq 0$ and $x+1 \geq 0$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m In this case, both $x-7$ and $x+1$ are non-negative, so the equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$x-7 = x+1$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Subtract $x$ from both sides to get:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$-7 = 1$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This is a contradiction, so there are no solutions for this case.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 3: Case 2: $x-7 < 0$ and $x+1 < 0$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m In this case, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$-(x-7) = -(x+1)$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Simplify the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$-x + 7 = -x - 1$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Subtract $-x$ from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$7 = -1$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Yes, this is a contradiction, so there are no solutions for this case either.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Note: If we have two cases with equal 2nd binomial, we need to add arbitrary constants to reach the equation.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So, in TOTAL there are no solutions for $|x-7| = |x+1|$.
