[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m [The Syhmtylum Company issued a five-year bond on January 1, 2017. The bonds have a par value of $1,000 per bond, make semiannual interest payments on July 1 and January 1, and mature on January 1, 2037. The company pays $72 per bond per year. Yearly yields on similar investments are 7%, 6%, and 8%, respectively. Compound interest is not computed, and interest is paid over the life of the bonds, with real interest included. The bonds were sold for $1,100 per bond. Compute the interest income to be recorded on July 1, 2017.]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To compute the interest expense for the interest income to be recorded on July 1, 2017, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. **Determine the total interest expense over the life of the bonds:**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - The bonds have a semiannual payment, so there are 10 semiannual periods (5 years * 2).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - The semiannual interest payment is $72.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - The effective semiannual yield is the annual yield minus the coupon rate for each bond.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - The annual yield for a bond with semiannual payments is calculated as:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      \text{Annual Yield} = \left( \frac{72}{1000} \right) \times \left( \frac{10}{6} \right) + \left( \frac{72}{1000} \right) \times \left( \frac{3}{6} \right) = \frac{0.72}{6} + \frac{0.72}{6} = \frac{1.44}{6} = 0.24 \text{ or } 24\%
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - The effective semiannual yield is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      \text{Effective Semiannual Yield} = 24\% - 7\% = 17\%
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - The annual interest rate is 7%, so the semiannual interest rate is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      \text{Semiannual Interest Rate} = \frac{7\%}{2} = 3.5\%
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - The interest expense for each semiannual period is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      \text{Interest Expense} = 1000 \times 0.035 = 35
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - The interest expense for a 10-period bond (\(35 \times 10 = 350\))
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Over 10 periods, the total interest expense is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      \text{Total Interest Expense} = 350 \times 10 = 3500
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. **Calculate the interest income for July 1, 2017:**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Compute for the semiannual interest income and add it to the total interest expense.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      \text{Interest Income} = 3500 \times (1 + 0.17) - 3500 = 3500 \times 1.17 - 3500 = 4105 - 3500 = 505
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, the interest income to be recorded on July 1, 2017, is \(\boxed{505}\).<|endoftext|>
