[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m In order to find the area when the radius is doubled, we need to calculate the effect on the area. Let's call the original radius  $\pi$  and the new radius  3$\pi$ . The original area of the circle inside the circle would be $(\pi)^2($by the formula of the Volume/Volume formula of the cylinder)*2^n for n equals the number of squares of the circle around the radius, which is $4$. On the other hand, the area with e-hodding is equal to the original radius... Right. So the new area would be "this" 3$\pi$ raised by "this", the original radius of n **.  ________$(^{|_^|}$   
