[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Yeah sure!
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m OK people, first some pre-prerequisites. This problem can be solved
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m more simply using Vieta's formulas. Indeed, the set of  $(x,y,z)$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m expressions you're given actually pretty much exactly matches the
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m solutions provided by Vieta's rules.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m These are attempting to link together the statements $1+(-9)=10$,
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $1-(-8)=9$ and $19-1=20^2$ in different ways. Reviewing Vieta's
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m formulae should let you solve this further by inferring that it
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m is actually possible (both procedurally and  intuitively) to
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m link 10 equations together in the process of forming the
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m a set of no fewer than four equations:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$ x + y - z = 10 \\ x - y + z = 9 \\ x - z + y = 20$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m with a view to turning into expressions for $z$, $x$ and $y$ only. To
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m establish these relationships you can also use rational proofs for
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m the squares and cube roots of complex numbers:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m x^2 - 10x + 9 & = \frac{1}{4}(x - 4)^2 \tag{a}\\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m x^2 - 9x + 20 & = \frac{1}{4}(x - 19)^2 \tag{b}\\
