[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m How many real numbers $x$ are solutions to the following equation? \[ |x-1| = |x-2| + |x-3| \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To solve the equation $|x-1| = |x-2| + |x-3|$,we can break it down into cases.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Case 1: Suppose $x > 3$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m In this case, the equation becomes $x-1 = x-2 + (x-3)$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Simplifying, we get $x-1 = x-2 + x-3$. Therefore, $1=x-2$, which means $x=3$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Case 2: Suppose $2\leq x \leq 3$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m In this case, $\text{written in two cases:}$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Case 2.1: $x-1=x-2+(x-3)$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We can simplify this to $x-1=x-2+x-3$, which gives $1=x$, and thus $x=1$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Case 2.2: $2\leq 3-x\leq 3$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since $3-x \leq 3$, this simplifies to $x \geq -1$. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Finally, we conclude that the solutions to the left side of the equation are all $x>3$ and all $1\leq x\leq 3$. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, the solutions to the equation are $\boxed{3, 3, 3, 3}$.
