[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - $235_7$ in base 10 is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      - We need to multiply each number by the corresponding base with which it is multiplied. From left to right, we have $i \cdot 7^2$, $i \cdot 7^1$, and $i \cdot 7^0$. In this case, $i = 2$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      - So the calculation is as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m        - $2 \cdot 7^2 = 2 \cdot 49 = 98$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m        - $3 \cdot 7^1 = 3 \cdot 7 = 21$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m        - $5 \cdot 7^0 = 5 \cdot 1 = 5$. Adding these together gives us $98 + 21 + 5 = 124$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Therefore, $235_7 = 124_{10}$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - $1324_5$ in base 10 is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      - We need to multiply each number by the corresponding base with which it is multiplied.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      - From left to right, we have $i \cdot 5^2$, $i \cdot 5^1$, and $i \cdot 5^0$. In this case, $i = 1$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      - So the calculation is as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m        - $1 \cdot 5^2 = 1 \cdot 25 = 25$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m        - $3 \cdot 5^1 = 3 \cdot 5 = 15$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m        - $2 \cdot 5^0 = 2 \cdot 1 = 2$. Adding these together gives us $25 + 15 + 2 = 42$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Therefore, $1324_5 = 42_{10}$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. Add the two base 10 numbers:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - $124 + 42 = 166$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. Convert the result back to base 10:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Base 10number $166$ is converted by dividing it by powers of 10 as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      - First, we divide $166$ by $10^1 = 1$ to get $166$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      - Next, we divide $166$ by $10^2 = 10$ to get $16$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m      - Finally, we divide $16$ by $10^3 = 1000$ to get $0.16$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Therefore, $166_{10} = 16_{10}$.
