[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. If $x = 2$, then $y = 10.5$, not an integer
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. If $x = 3$, then $y = 6.333\ldots$, not an integer
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 4. ...
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 5. If $x = 21$, then $y = 1$, not a leap year (not 60 years)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 6. If $x = 1$ and $x \cdot y = 21$, then $y = 21$, which is an integer but not composite (not needed)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 7. If $x = 21$ and $x \cdot y = 21$, then $y = 1$, but not a leap year (not needed)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Continuing this iteration, we find that the smallest composite number that meets the criteria is $n = 30$. Therefore, the number of distinct prime factors of $n$ is:
