[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2003 (binary: 1110011001)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, we will divide 2003 by 11. We divide one divisor (11) aka our 11-bit number, and the other dividend (2003), until we reach 0, leaving us with the remainders. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2003 ÷ 11 ≈ 181.0909, with a remainder 1. This means that when we end up with 20, we'll have 11 remainders: 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - 2003 divided by 11 is a **decimal remainder** which is 20.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - 20 % 11 is 10 (meaning 10 is a remainder)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So, when we divide 2003 by 11, we can get to the next quotient, \(181\), appending the remainder obtained during the process. That means zhhh,
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
