[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - For \( x \ge 0 \), we have \( f(x) = x^3 - 5 \), which approaches infinity as \( x \to 0^+ \).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To determine the range of \( f(x) \):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - Since \( x^3 - 5 \to \infty \) as \( x \to 0^+ \), all values of \( x \) greater than zero must be less than or equal to 0 (to avoid \( x^3 - 5 \) being undefined).
