[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \theta_2 = \pi + (-2\pi) = -\pi
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \theta_2 = \pi - \pi = 0
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 4. **Calculate the difference \(\theta_1 - \theta_2\)**:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \theta_1 - \theta_2 = 3\pi - 0 = 3\pi
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 5. **Calculate the distance \(AB\)**:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    Using the distance formula for two points in polar coordinates:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    AB = \sqrt{(r_2 - r_1)^2 + (d\cos\theta_1 - d\sin\theta_1)^2}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    Here, \( r_2 = 9 \), \( r_1 = 3 \), and \( d = 9 \cdot \cos(3\pi) - 9\sin(3\pi) = 9 \cdot (-1) - 9 = -9 \).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So, substitute in the values:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m AB = \sqrt{(9 - 3)^2 + (-9\sin(3\pi) - (-9) \sin(3\pi / 2))^2}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m AB = \sqrt{6^2 + (9(-1) - (-9)(-1))^2} = \sqrt{36 + (9(-1) - (9)(-1))^2} = \sqrt{36 + (-18)} = \sqrt{18} = 3\sqrt{2}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Let's confirm this calculation using Python functions to ensure accuracy.
