[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m If $a\equiv 16\pmod{37}$ and $b\equiv 21\pmod{37}$, then for what integer $n$ in the set $\{0,1,2,\ldots,35,36\}$ is it true that $$a-b\equiv n\pmod{37}~?$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To solve this, we consider the given congruences:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ a \equiv 16 \pmod{37} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ b \equiv 21 \pmod{37} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We want to find an integer \( n \) in the set \(\{0, 1, 2, \ldots, 35, 36\}\) such that:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ a - b \equiv n \pmod{37} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Let's write the congruences uniquely:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ a = 37k + 16 \quad \text{for some integer } k \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ b = 37m + 21 \quad \text{for some integer } m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now we want to express \( a - b \):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ a - b = (37k + 16) - (37m + 21) = 37(k - m) + 16 - 21 = 37(k - m) - 5 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We need \( 37(k - m) - 5 \equiv n \pmod{37} \). Here, \( n \) is the remainder when \( 37(k - m) - 5 \) is divided by 37. Since \( 37(k - m) \) is a multiple of 37, it doesn't contribute to \( n \) modulo 37. We solely need the remainder when \(-5\) is divided by 37:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ -5 \equiv 37 \cdot 13 \pmod{37} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This is because subtracting a multiple of the modulus (here, 37) from a multiple of the modulus doesn't change the value modulo 37.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Thus, \( n \equiv 37 \cdot 13 \pmod{37} \):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ n \equiv 489 \pmod{37} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ n \equiv 39 \pmod{37} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ n = 39 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So the answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \boxed{39}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
