[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*} \tan 75^\circ &= \frac{\sin 75^\circ}{\cos 75^\circ} \\ &= \frac{\frac{\sqrt{6} + \sqrt{2}}{4}}{\frac{\sqrt{6} - \sqrt{2}}{4}} \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\tan 75^\circ$ represents tangent of an angle $75^\circ.$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\tan 75^\circ  =$ \frac{\cos 75^\circ}{\sin 75^\circ}.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Let us convert $\sin 75^\circ$ {} $\cos 75^\circ$ to $\sin 50^\circ$ {} $\cos 50^\circ$ and $\sin 30^\circ$ where $75^\circ = 60^\circ + 15^\circ = 50^\circ$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\sin 50^\circ = \cos 50^\circ = \sin (180^\circ - 50^\circ) = \sin 130^\circ$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*} \tan 75^\circ  &= \frac{\sin 75^\circ}{\cos 75^\circ} \\ &= \frac{\frac{\sqrt{6} + \sqrt{2}}{4}}{\frac{\sqrt{6} - \sqrt{2}}{4}} \\ &=\frac{\sqrt{6} + \sqrt{2}}{\sqrt{6} - \sqrt{2}} \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Evaluate the expression and simplify.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Find a common denominator.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $4(\sqrt{6} - \sqrt{2}) = {4(\sqrt{6} - \sqrt{2})} \times {4(\sqrt{6} + \sqrt{2})}  = 16(\sqrt{6} - \sqrt{2})(\sqrt{6} + \sqrt{2}).$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\sqrt{6}^2$ and $\sqrt{2}^2$ are $12$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Substitute this factorization.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\tan 75^\circ$ simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*} \tan 75^\circ &= \frac{(\sqrt{6} - \sqrt{2})(\sqrt{6} + \sqrt{2})}{\sqrt{6}  - \sqrt{2}} \\ &= \frac{\sqrt{6}^2 - (\sqrt{2})^2}{\sqrt{6} - \sqrt{2}} \\ &= \frac{6 - 2}{\sqrt{6} - \sqrt{2}} \\ &= \frac{4}{\sqrt{6} - \sqrt{2}} \\ &= \frac{4 (\sqrt{6} + \sqrt{2})}{(\sqrt{6} - \sqrt{2})(\sqrt{6} + \sqrt{2})} \\ &= \frac{4 \sin (180^\circ - 50^\circ)}{(\sqrt{6})^2 - (\sqrt{2})^2} \\ &= \frac{4 \cos 50^\circ}{3} \\ &= \frac{2}{\cos 50^\circ} \\ &= 2 \sec 50^\circ \\ \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Thus, the value of $\tan 75^\circ$ is $2 \sec 50^\circ.$<|endoftext|>
