[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First, we need to find the projection matrix $\mathbf{P}$ onto the vector $\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}.$  Recall that the projection matrix onto a vector $\begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \end{pmatrix}$ is given by $(1-a)(1-b)\mathbf{I}.$  In this case, we have $a = -3$ and $b = -2.$  Thus, the projection matrix is
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$\mathbf{P} = \begin{pmatrix} 1-(-3) & 1-(-2) \\ 1-(-3) & 1-(-2) \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 & 3 \\ 4 & 3 \end{pmatrix}.$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The formula for the \textit{inverse} of a matrix $\mathbf{A}$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\mathbf{A}^{-1} = \frac{1}{\det(\mathbf{A})}( \det(\mathbf{A})\mathbf{I} - \mathbf{A}( \mathbf{A}^{-1} ) )$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Using $ 4+3 \neq 0$ to determine the determinant, we find
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*}\det(\mathbf{P}) &= 4 \cdot 3 - 3 \cdot 4 \\ &= 12 -12 \\ &= 0 \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Thus, we know that
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$\mathbf{P}^{-1} = \frac{1}{0}( \det(\mathbf{P})\mathbf{I} - \mathbf{P}\mathbf{I} )$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$\mathbf{P}^{-1} = \frac{1}{0}\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix} -3 & 6 \\ -10 & 26 \end{pmatrix}$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$\mathbf{P}^{-1} = \boxed{\text{Zero matrix}}$$<|endoftext|>
