[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Ali is a logger. His job is to cut down as many trees as possible and then sell the money to buy lumber. He also has to pay taxes and to also be able to show proof that he cut down the maximum number of trees to be eligible for a federal tax law change that would decrease the tax burden for him by 20%. He is eligible for the federal tax law change because the value of a tree is about $150. How many trees does he cut down to remain eligible for the tax change? To work out how many trees Ali needs to cut down to remain eligible for the tax change because the value of a tree is about $150. We can do this by dividing the cost of the log by the amount they are going to be taxed, and then multiply the result by the number of trees he can cut down.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To remain eligible for the federal tax law change because the value of a tree is about $150. We can also come up with the following steps:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ \text{Number of trees to remain eligible (elementary fact calculation) } = \frac{150}{20\%} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Let's compute this step by step using Python.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m # Define the cost of a log, the tax rate (in percent), and the tax rate for cut-out trees
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m cost_of_log = 150  # in dollars
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m tax_rate = 0.2  # in percent
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m tax_rate_for_cut_trees = tax_rate - 10  # because 10% per day needs to be lowered to 0%
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m # Calculate the number of trees to remain eligible
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m number_of_trees_to_remain_eligible = cost_of_log / tax_rate_for_cut_trees
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m print(number_of_trees_to_remain_eligible)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m ```
