[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We want to factor $w^4-16$ as far as possible, where this allows us to express it as $w^4-(2w)^4$. Expanding, we are left with the expression $w^4-16w^4+16w^4-64w^4+64w^4$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$(2w)^4+64w^4=[(2w)^2-64w^2][(2w)^2+64w^2]$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Factorize each expression separately:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$(2w)^2-64w^2=(2w-8w)(2w+8w)=-8w(2w-8w)$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$(2w)^2+64w^2=(2w+8w)(2w-8w)=10w(2w-8w)$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Putting it all together, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$w^4-16w^4+16w^4-64w^4+64w^4=(w-8w)(-(8w-2w))(w+8w)(-(2w-8w))$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Simplify the expression inside each parentheses:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$w^4-16w^4=16w^4$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$16w^4-64w^4=-48w^4$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$ 64w^4+64w^4=(2w)^4$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So we can write the final answer as:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$w^4-16w^4+16w^4-64w^4+64w^4=(2w-8w)(-(8w-2w))(w+8w)(-(2w-8w))$$
