[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We can optimize the expression by expressing it differently:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m (a+b+c+d)^{2} + (e+f+g+h)^{2} = (a+b+c+d+(e+f+g+h))(a+b+c+d-(e+f+g+h))
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \(a+b+c+d\) and \((e+f+g+h)\) are both perfect squares. Given that none of them equals \(-7\) in the given set, we can set \(a+b+c+d = 13\) and \(e+f+g+h = 7\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Substituting these values in, the expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m (13-7)(13+7) = 6 \cdot 20 = \boxed{120}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
