[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m What is the degree measure of the supplement of the complement of a 42-degree angle?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To calculate the degree measure of the supplement of the complement of a 42-degree angle, we need to follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 1: Find the complement of the given angle.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The complement of an angle is equal to 90 degrees minus the given angle. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Complement of 42 degrees = 90 degrees - 42 degrees
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 2: Calculate the supplement of the complement.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The supplement of an angle is equal to 180 degrees minus the given angle.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Supplement of complement of 42 degrees = 180 degrees - 90 degrees
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 3: Simplify the outcome.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Supplement of complement of 42 degrees = 90 degrees
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The degree measure of the supplement of the complement of a 42-degree angle is 90 degrees.
