[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Sandy plans to paint one wall in her bedroom. The wall is 9 feet high and 12 feet long. There is a 2-foot by 4-foot area on that wall that she will not have to paint due to the window. How many square feet will she need to paint?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Sure! Let's break down the steps to determine how many square feet Sandy needs to paint on her wall.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. **Calculate the area of the entire wall:**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \text{Area of the entire wall} = \text{height} \times \text{length}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    The wall is 9 feet high and 12 feet long:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \text{Area} = 9 \, \text{feet} \times 12 \, \text{feet} = 108 \, \text{square feet}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. **Calculate the area of the window area:**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \text{Area of the window} = \text{length} \times \text{width}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    The window is 2 feet wide and 4 feet tall:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \text{Area} = 4 \, \text{feet} \times 2 \, \text{feet} = 8 \, \text{square feet}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. **Subtract the area of the window from the total area of the entire wall:**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \text{Free area to paint} = \text{Area of the entire wall} - \text{Area of the window}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \text{Free area} = 108 \, \text{square feet} - 8 \, \text{square feet} = 100 \, \text{square feet}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 4. **Subtract the free area to get the actual painted area:**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \text{Applicable area to paint} = \text{Total area of the wall} - \text{Free area to paint}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \text{Applicable area to paint} = 108 \, \text{square feet} - 100 \, \text{square feet} = 8 \, \text{square feet}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, Sandy will need to paint \boxed{8} square feet on her wall.<|endoftext|>
