[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Let $AB$ be a diameter of a circle centered at $O$.  Let $E$ be a point on the circle, and let the tangent at $B$ intersect the tangent at $E$ and $AE$ at $C$ and $D$, respectively.  If $\angle BAE = 43^\circ$, find $\angle CED$, in degrees.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
