[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First, let's calculate the remainder when 1111 is divided by 9.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1111 \div 9 = 123 \text{ remainder } 4
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This means:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1111 = 9 \times 123 + 4
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So, the remainder when 1111 is divided by 9 is 4. Therefore,:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m -1111 \equiv -4 \pmod {9}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Next, we need to find a positive integer \( n \) such that:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m -4 \equiv n \pmod{9}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We can convert \(-4\) to a positive equivalent by adding 9:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m -4 + 9 = 5
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Thus, we find that:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m -4 \equiv 5 \pmod {9}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, the integer \( n \) that satisfies both conditions, \( 0 \le n < 9 \) and \( -1111 \equiv n \pmod {9} \), is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
