[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m What is the domain of the function $f(x)=\log_2(\log_3(\log_4(\log_5x)))$?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To determine the domain of the function \( f(x) = \log_2(\log_3(\log_4(\log_5x))) \), we need to find the values of \( x \) for which the expression inside the logarithms is defined. The logarithm function is only defined for positive arguments. Therefore, we need to solve the inequalities:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{cases} 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \log_3(\log_4(\log_5x)) > 0 & \text{(since } \log_4(x) > 0\text{ implies } x > 1 \text{ and } \log_5(x) > 0 \text{ implies } x > 1.5\text{, but } x > 1\text{ cannot overlap with } \log_4(x) > 0 \text{ since } \log_5(x) > \log_3(\log_4(x)) > \log_4(|x|) > 0.5 \text{)} 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m }\end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This translates to:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{cases} 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \log_3(x) > 1 & \text{(since } x > 1.5\text{, and } \log_4(1.5) < \log_4(1) = 0\text{, infimum for } \log_4(x) \text{ is } 1\text{)} \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \log_5(x) > 1.5 & \text{(since } x > 1\text{)}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This gives us:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{cases} 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m x > 3 \text{ and } 5^1.5 > x \implies x < e^1.5 > 4.8177 \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m x > 3 \text{ and } 5 \cdot 1.5^2 > x \implies 2.5 > x
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So, the domain of the function is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m (3, e^1.5)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \boxed{(3, e^1.5)}<|endoftext|>
