[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We will begin by solving the equation $9x^3=4x^2$ to get a system of equations for $x$ and $y$, where $y$ is some expression involving $x$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \\ \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline x^3+4x^2&9x^3&4x^2&0&4&4x^2&9x^3\hline x^3+4x^2-(y+9x^3)=0&x^2+(4+3y)x+4x^{2+y}&2y+3y^{2+2y}=4x^{2+y}&0&0&4x^{2+y+3y}=9x^{3+y}&x^2+4x(y+9)=0&&&&\\hline 3(x+y)^2&6y+9x+y^{2+y}=0&&&&&&&&\\hline \\end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since $x$ and $y$ are real numbers, we know that $3(x+y)^2=0$ and $6y+9x+y^{2+2y}=0$. Let $a=x+y$ and $b=y+2y^2$. Then, we have the equation $ab=1$ in $R^3$. One obvious solution is the origin $(0,0,0)$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
