[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Yes, I understand. To solve for \( x \) in the equation \((17^6 - 17^5) \div 16 = 17^x\), let’s follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. Simplify both sides of the equation.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \begin{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \text{(Simplified side)} &= (17^6 - 17^5) 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \end{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    Notice that \( (a^b - a^c) \) can be factored in a way related to \( a \) raised to an exponent of higher terms.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. Hint: Watch how the terms on both sides of the equation interact to show a relationship involving repeated squaring by powers of 17.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \begin{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    (a^b - a^c) &= a^b(a^c - 1) \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    (a^b - a^c) \div a^c &= a^b\left(\frac{a^c - 1}{a^c}\right)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \end{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. Observe the bottom part of the left-hand side of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    (a^b - a^c) \div a^c = a^b \left(\frac{a^c - 1}{a^c}\right) 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    Simplify this further to match \((a^b - a^c) \div a^c\):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \begin{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    (a^b - a^c) \div a^c &= a^b \left(\frac{a^c - 1}{a^c}\right) \\[6pt]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    &= a^b \times 1 \quad \text{(cancel common terms)} \\[6pt]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    &\Rightarrow a^b - 1 \\[6pt]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \end{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 4. Now rewrite the original equation with this factored form:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    (17^6 - 17^5) \div 16 = (17^6 - 17^5) \div 16 = \frac{17^6 - 17^5}{16}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    Using our rewritten factor of 17:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    17^6 - 17^5 = (17^3)^2 - (17^2)^2
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    Factorize further:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    17^6 - 17^5 = 17^5(17^1 - 17) 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    Next, note that since \(17^1 - 17 = 17 - 17\):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    17^1 - 17 = 0
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
