[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m If $\mathbf{A} = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix},$ then its transpose is given by
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\mathbf{A}^T = \begin{pmatrix} a & c \\ b & d \end{pmatrix}.\]Given that $\mathbf{A}^T = \mathbf{A}^{-1},$ find $a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + d^2.$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\mathbf{A}^T = \begin{pmatrix} a & c \\ b & d \end{pmatrix},$ a transpose $=$ b inverse $=$ d inverse $=$ c inverse
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\therefore \mathrm{tr}\(\mathbf{A}\) = a+ d$ and $\mathrm{tr}\(\mathbf{A}^T\)= a+ d$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m so $a+d=b+d, $a=c+d,$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m both of the rows of the matrix are the same $=$ b=c
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + d^2 = a^2 + d^2 + b^2 + c^2 + b^2 + c^2 = 2(a^2 + b^2 + c^2 +d^2) = 2(a+d)^2=2(a+c)^2=2d^2$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m But there is no solution with diffrent $d^2.$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m DAQAOADRXS
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m As u know, $\mathbf A^T = \mathbf A^{-1}$ so the condition means that $AA^TA^{-1}A^T = I = AA^TA^TT^{-1}}$<|endoftext|>
