[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find out how many dollars Kirsty owes the plumber, we need to calculate the total cost based on both the hourly rate and the equipment unit cost.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. **Convert units to base 10 (10)**:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Plumber charges $242_5$ dollars for every hour of labor.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Plumber charges $367_{8}$ dollars for equipment.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - ($242_5$ in base 10 = $242 \times 10^0 + 5 \times 10^1$ = $242 + 5$ = $247$).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - ($367_{8}$ in base 10 = $3 \times 8^2 + 6 \times 8^1 + 7 \times 8^0 = 3 \times 64 + 6 \times 8 + 7$ = $192 + 48 + 7$ = $247$).
