[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the probability that exactly two out of four dice show an even number, we can use the binomial probability formula. Let's go step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First, determine the probability that a single die shows an even number. There are 10 even numbers out of 20 possible numbers:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m p_even = 10 / 20 = 0.5
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Next, determine the probability that a single die does not show an even number. Then, multiply this probability by itself three times (for the other three dice):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
