[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m When a car's brakes are applied, it travels 5 feet less in each  second than the previous second until it comes to a complete stop.  A car goes 45 feet in the first second after the brakes are applied.  How many feet does the car travel from the time the  brakes are applied to the time the car stops?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To calculate the distance a car travels from the time the brakes are applied to the time when it stops, we need to understand its motion situation.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m **First Second:** The car travels 45 feet.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m **At First Second:** At the first second, the car is at its maximum distance from stopping because the brakes will cause it to stop immediately after the first second. So, it travels 45 feet straight.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m **From First Second to Halfway Between Stop and Stop:** The car travels 45 feet for the first second. At this point, the total distance the car travels is 45 feet for 2 seconds.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m **Halfway Between Stop and Stop:** At the halfway point, the car travels two more first seconds of 45 feet. The total distance the car travels now is 90 feet.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m **At Halfway Between Stop and Stop:** At the second half of the fifth second, the car is still on the way to stopping. The total distance the car travels will now be measured at the end of the fifth second. Since the car stopped at the halfway point at 19.825 feet (which is \((2 \times 45 - 5 + 1) = 19.825\) feet), we can conclude that the car stops 19.825 feet away.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Voila! So, 19 feet is the total distance the car travels till it ends in a stop.
