[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Solve the congruence $11n \equiv 7 \pmod{43}$, as a residue modulo 43.  (Give an answer between 0 and 42.)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We need to solve \newline{\begin{align*}\vline {\displaystyle 11n\equiv 7 \pmod{43}}& \vline \\n& \end{align*}}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m In order to solve this congruence equation, we will first look for the initial process of finding the solution. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Notice that 11 and 43 are relatively prime numbers, which means their greatest common divisor (gcd) is 1. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Using the property of congruence, we start with the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \newline{\begin{align*}11n \equiv 7 \pmod{43} \end{align*}}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We are given that $\gcd(11, 43) = 1$, so we can safely simplify our equation to
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \newline{\begin{align*}n \equiv 7 \pmod{43} \end{align*}}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This means that there exists a unique integer $n$ between 0 and 42, inclusive, that satisfies the congruence equation.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m But we need to find a remainder when $n$ is divided by 43, which corresponds to the remainder when 7 is divided by 43. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Thus, the condition $11n \equiv 7 \pmod{43}$ will be satisfied for a unique value of $n$ in the range of 0 to 42.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, the answer is $\boxed{7}$ (between 0 and 42).iotic.<|endoftext|>
