[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To determine the value of \(a\) in the equation \(y = ax^2 + bx + c\) given the graph, we need to use the vertex form of a quadratic equation, which is \(y = a(x - h)^2 + k\), where \((h, k)\) is the vertex of the parabola.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m From the graph:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - The vertex of the parabola is at \((1, 1)\), so \(h = 1\) and \(k = 1\).
