[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Let's analyze this problem: we want to find how many even 3-digit numbers have the digit sum of the tens and units digits equal to 10.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To do this, we first figure out what all the possibilities are for a 3-digit number with a digit sum of 10. There are 9 ways to get a digit sum of 10: 9, 8+1, 7+2, 6+3, 5+4, 4+5, 3+6, 2+7, and the sum of 2 or 3.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Let's look at each one individually: 9, 8 + 1 is 10; 7 + 2 is 9; 6 + 3 is 9; 5 + 4 is 9; 4 + 5 is 9; 3 + 6 is 9; 2 + 7 is 9; 5 + 4 + 1 is 10 (only 5 + 4 and 4 + 5 are not even numbers); 5 + 7 + 1 is 13 (not 10) 8 + 8 is 16 (not 10)! 6 + 6 + 4, not 10! So only 7 + 2 and the two 8 - these two numbers will be the even numbers where the digit sum of the tens and units digits is 10! Let's figure out what all the possible 2-digit numbers have a digit sum of 10.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Those 2-digit numbers are 10, 29, 38, 47, 56, 65, 74, 83, 92.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m For each of those, we have 10 subtracting from 99 to get a single 2-digit number with a digit sum of 10: 98, 97, 96, 95, 94, and 91.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Thus, there are 8 possible 2-digit numbers that are missing: the digit sum of the tens digit is 10 i.e. 90 and 90 + 1 is 10.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Let's add, for each of them, the rest numbers we know (which, all 2- and 3-digit numbers from the start).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m For 90 + 1, from the first 99 numbers, + 98 is the 8-20 number, + 97 is the 8-19 number, + 96 is the 8-18 number - etc. from 101 numbers (50), + 95 is the 8-17 number, +...
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Thus, the 8 numbers are 8+1 since 89 + 1= 90.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m For the 19 - 20 numbers, they just reset to 90! 6 beginning numbers that are not diff by 10 have a digit sum of 10 i.e. 18, 17, 16, ..., 89 - is the 19-17 number.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, there are 18 + 8 = 26 numbers and for 29 I'll note as its properties to avoid counting again/one more count: 88, 87, 79, 78, 77, 76 (if the problem say for 29 also 79+8 = 10 efficient when you multiply the number by 8), 76, 75, 74, 73, 72, 71, 81, 80+1 =91 is the 29-0, 89= 10 efficient when you multiply the number by 10), 68, 67, 66, 65 (if the problem say for 29 also 66+7 = 10 efficient when you multiply the number by 7), 65, 64, 63, 62, 61, 70, 73, 72 (if the problem say for 29 also 70+6 = 10 efficient when you multiply the number by 6), 58, 57, 56 (if the problem say for 29 also 57+8 = 10 efficient when you multiply the number by 8), 56, 55, 54, 53, 52, 51, 61, 62, 63, 64, 65, 66, 67, 68, 69, 72 (if the problem say for 29 also 69+6 = 10 efficient when you multiply the number by 6), 48, 47, 46, 45, 44, 43 (if the problem say for 29 also 47+8 = 10 efficient when you multiply the number by 8), 46, 45, 44, 43, 42, 5, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7, 7
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Then, I remember 73 for 28 since + 70 = 10) again I'll write as its properties to avoid counting again/one more count: 80, 71, 62, 53, 107 and 107 is odd. Holidays, Doomsday, or a great low! So that there is 10 way to skip  or under number even 3-digit numbers that satisfy the sum of 10.
