[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Let $\alpha$ and $\beta$ be complex numbers such that $|\beta| = 1$ and $\overline{\alpha} \beta \neq 1.$  Find the maximum value of
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\left| \frac{\beta - \alpha}{1 - \overline{\alpha} \beta} \right|.\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The given expression is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \left| \frac{\beta - \alpha}{1 - \overline{\alpha} \beta} \right|
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We can use the definition of the modulus (or absolute value) of a complex number to simplify this expression. The absolute value of a complex number \\(x + yi\\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m |x + yi| = \sqrt{x^2 + y^2}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, we can simplify our expression as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \left| \frac{\beta - \alpha}{1 - \overline{\alpha} \beta} \right| = \left| \frac{\beta - \alpha}{1 - \overline{\alpha} \beta} \right| = \frac{\left| \beta - \alpha \right|}{\left| 1 - \overline{\alpha} \beta \right|}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
