[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First, let's find the radius of each golf ball. By using the Pythagorean theorem, we can find the radius of the circular segments delimited from the corners of the box and the midpoint of the box to circle, and find the radii of the circular segments delimited from the corners of the box and the outer ends of the box to balls.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Method 1:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. \\(r_{seg} = \dfrac {\sqrt {13.5^{2}-4^{2}}}2\\)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. \\(r_{ball} = 2R - r_{seg}\\)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Method 2:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \\(r_{ball} = \dfrac {R-0.5}{2}\)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Method 3:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. \\(r_{seg} = \dfrac {\sqrt {13.5^{2}-4^{2}}}2\\)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. \\(r_{ball} = 2R - r_{seg}\\)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
