[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m My school's math club has 6 boys and 8 girls.  I need to select a team to send to the state math competition.  We want 6 people on the team.  In how many ways can I select the team without restrictions?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To select a team of 6 people without any restrictions, we can use the combination formula, which is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m C(n, k) = n! / (k!(n-k)!)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m where:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m n is the total number of people (6 boys and 8 girls)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m k is the number of people we want to choose (6)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Plugging in the values, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m C(6, 6) = 6! / (6!(6-6)!)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m C(6, 6) = 6! / (6! * 0!)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m C(6, 6) = 1
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, there is only 1 way to select a team of 6 people without any restrictions.<|endoftext|>
