[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m A fair coin is flipped 7 times.  What is the probability that at least 5 of the flips come up heads?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Yes, thank you.@ Nice! Here's how we can solve the problem step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We want to find the probability that at least 5 of the 7 tosses of a fair coin come up heads.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We can use the Binomial formula to find the probability of getting exactly k heads out of n tosses. The Binomial formula is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$P(X=k)=\frac{(n)_k}{n^k} \times p^k \times (1-p)^{n-k}$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Where \(P(X = k)\) is the probability of getting exactly \(k\) heads.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m In this case, \(n = 7\) (number of tosses), \(k\) can be 5, 6, or 7 (any number from 5 to 7 inclusive), and \(p = \frac{1}{2}\) (probability of a flip coming up heads).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The Formula becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$P(X=5) = \frac{(7)_5}{7^5} \times \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^5 \times \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{7-5}$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$P(X=6) = \frac{(7)_6}{7^6} \times \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^6 \times \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{7-6}$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$P(X=7) = \frac{(7)_7}{7^7} \times \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^7 \times \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{7-7}$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So we can simplify it:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$P(X=5) = \frac{126}{16800} \times \frac{1}{64} \times \frac{1}{16} = \frac{11}{11552000}$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$P(X=6) = \frac{300}{27993600} \times \frac{1}{64} \times \frac{1}{8} = \frac{375}{1215214720}$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$P(X=7) = \frac{840}{1680019200} \times \frac{1}{64} \times \frac{1}{16} = \frac{210}{10036266160}$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We can now find the sum of these probabilities:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$P(X\geq 5) = P(X=5) + P(X=6) + P(X=7)$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To sum these probabilities, we can use a simple addition:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$P(X\geq 5) = \frac{11}{11552000} + \frac{375}{1215214720} + \frac{210}{10036266160}$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$P(X\geq 5) = \frac{240}{815037280}$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So the probability that at least 5 of the 7 rolls will come up heads is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$\boxed{\frac{240}{815037280}}$$<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m [Ground Truth]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \frac{29}{128}
