[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We can further split this into two cases based on their respective squares.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. When \(y > 1\), \(y^2 > 1\). Hence, \(|y - 1| = y - 1\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. When \(y < -1\), \(y^2 < 1\). Therefore, \(|y - 1| = -(y - 1)\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, we look at the possible values provided by the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*}
