[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. Since both \(x\) and \(y\) must satisfy \(\left|x + 2y - 4\right| = 0\) and \(x = 1\) and \(x = 3\), a clear contradiction arises because \(x = 1\) and \(x = 3\) cannot independently satisfy both conditions simultaneously. This contradiction indicates an error in the problem setup or a misunderstanding of the problem. However, we can use another source of knowledge that might confirm our solutions.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 4. Use the properties of quadratic equations to solve the system.
