[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First, since Fred and Gwen must sit opposite each other, we can represent their sitting arrangement as F- (Fred)G-WG. This suffix means that Fred must be seated somewhere between Gwen and Gwen opposite Fred. This leaves us with 3 other slots to fill for the remaining seats with the other 4 people.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m For Fred, there are 3 choices (he could sit in any of the 3 slots after Gwen). For Gwen, there are 2 choices (since they must sit opposite each other).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We then have 4 slots left for the remaining people (the rest of the seatings we consider is Guan).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The number of ways to arrange the remaining people is 4P4 which is 4!
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Thus, the total number of seating arrangements where Fred & Gwen are not next to each other is 3 * 2*4 = 24.
