[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m If $p(x) = x^2 + 4x + 4$, then $p(-x) = (-x)^2 + 4(-x) + 4 = x^2 - 4x + 4 = (x - 2)^2$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Given that $p(x) > 0$ for all real numbers while $p(-x) > 0$, it follows that $(-x)^2 + 4(-x) + 4 > 0$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Hence, the inequality $p(x) < 0 \implies p(x) + p(-x) < 0$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, the range is $(-\infty, -2)$.
