[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Thank you for the explanation! I'll make it even simpler. The range of a function is the set of all possible output values of that function. For the function $p(x) = x^2 + 4x + 4$, we know that it can take any value on the x-axis. Since $p(-x) > 0$ for all x, it follows that $p(x) + p(-x) > 0$. Adding 4 to both sides, we get $p(x) > -2$. Therefore, the range is \boxed{(-\infty, -2)}.
