[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 1: Understand the problem
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We have to evaluate the absolute value of the complex number $-4+\frac{7}{6}i$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 2: Recall the absolute value of a complex number.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The absolute value (or modulus) of a complex number $a+bi$ is given by $|a+bi| = \sqrt{a^2 + b^2}$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 3: Apply the formula for complex numbers.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The complex number $-4+\frac{7}{6}i$ has the following components:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - Real part: $-4$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - Imaginary part: $\frac{7}{6}i$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 4: Calculate the square root of the sum of the squares of the real and imaginary parts.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Using the formula $|a+bi| = \sqrt{a^2 + b^2} ,we get $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m | -4 + \frac{7}{6}i | = \sqrt{(-4)^2 + \left(\frac{7}{6}\right)^2} = \sqrt{16 + \frac{49}{36}} = \sqrt{\frac{576}{36} + \frac{49}{36}} = \sqrt{\frac{625}{36}} = \frac{25}{6}$$
