[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ \cos 54^\circ \cos 4^\circ - \cos 36^\circ \cos 86^\circ \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First, let's simplify the product of the cosines involving 36 and 86:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ \cos 36^\circ \cos 86^\circ \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since $\cos 86^\circ = -\cos 7^\circ$, the product becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ \cos 36^\circ \cos 86^\circ = \cos 36^\circ (-\cos 7^\circ) = -\cos 36^\circ \cos 7^\circ \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, let's apply the new cosines identity involved here:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ \cos 54^\circ \cos 4^\circ - \cos 36^\circ \cos 86^\circ \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Using $\cos 36^\circ \cos 86^\circ = -\cos 36^\circ \cos 7^\circ$:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ \cos 54^\circ \cos 4^\circ - (-\cos 36^\circ \cos 7^\circ) \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ = \cos 54^\circ \cos 4^\circ + \cos 36^\circ \cos 7^\circ \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since $\cos 54^\circ = \cos (90^\circ - 36^\circ) = \sin 36^\circ$, we can rewrite $\cos 54^\circ$ as $\cos (90^\circ - 36^\circ) = \sin 36^\circ$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So the expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ \sin 36^\circ \sin 4^\circ + \cos 36^\circ \cos 7^\circ \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, let's notice that the expression can be further simplified using the sum-to-product identities, but this product can be handled in a more simplified form using the angle addition identities.
