[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Find the minimum value of $9^x - 3^x + 1$ over all real numbers $x.$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the minimum value of the expression $9^x - 3^x + 1$, we can start by examining when the expression is equal to 1, because setting it equal to 1, we can simplify the expression.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\begin{aligned} 9^x - 3^x &= 1 \\ (3^x)^2 - (3^x)^2 &= 1 \\ x(3^x - 3^x) &= 1 \\ x &= \frac{1}{3^x - 3^x} \end{aligned}$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We can check the value of this expression at the critical point where $3^x - 3^x = 1$. This happens when $x = 0$, which is the origin on the real number line.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So, we evaluate the expression at this point:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\lim_x\left(x = \frac{1}{3^x - 3^x}\right) = 0$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, $9^0 - 3^0 + 1 = 1 - 1 + 1 = 2$. This is the minimum value of the expression $9^x - 3^x + 1$ .
