[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. **Set up a system of equations representing the intersection of these parametric lines.**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. **Solve the system of equations to find the intersection point.**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m ### Step 1: Find the parametric equations of the lines \(AB\) and \(CD\)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m #### Line \(AB\):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - Point \(A = (6, -7, 7)\)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - Point \(B = (16, -17, 12)\)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The direction vector of line \(AB\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \vec{d}_{AB} = B - A = (16 - 6, -17 - (-7), 12 - 7) = (10, -10, 5)
