[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m and eliminate $(a - (b - 1)^{3})^{2}=a^{2}+(b - 1)^{6}-2a$, obtaining the equation $(3b - 4)^{2} = 4 - 3b^{2}\text{.}$ Thus, we get $b = 1$ or $(3b-5)^{2}=1$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m When $b =1$, $(4^x + 2^x - 6)^{3} = 1$. Thus, we have $4^x + 2^x - 6 = 0$. Moreover, $(2^x - 4)(2^x - 2) = 0$. Hence $x = 1$ or $x = 0$.
