[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m **Case 2: \( x \neq -1 \)**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The median is \(38\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m In this case, the median must be \(x\) because the median is the middle number when the numbers are arranged in ascending order.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The mean of the set is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \frac{12 + 38 + 45 + x + 14}{5} = \frac{109 + x}{5}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Setting the median equal to the mean:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \frac{12 + 38 + 45 + x + 14}{5} = \frac{109 + x}{5}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
