[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Five people can mow a lawn in 12 hours.  How many more people are needed to mow the lawn in just 3 hours, assuming each person mows at the same rate?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To solve this problem, we need to determine the rate at which each person mows the lawn and then calculate how many additional people are required to complete the work in 3 hours.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 1: Determine the rate of mowing.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The rate of mowing is the number of lawn yards that are mowed per hour. We can find this by dividing the original lawn mowing by the total number of hours. So, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Rate of mowing = (Number of people \times Number of lawn yards per person per hour) / Time
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Rate of mowing = (5 people \times 4000 square feet per hour) / 12 hours
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Rate of mowing = (20,000 square feet per hour) / 12 hours
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Rate of mowing = 1,666.67 square feet per hour
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 2: Calculate the amount of work required to be completed in 3 hours.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the amount of work required, we can multiply the rate of mowing by the time the work needs to be completed:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Work required = Rate of mowing \* Time
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Work required = 1,666.67 square feet per hour \* 3 hours
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Work required = 5,000 square feet
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 3: Determine the number of people needed to complete the work in 3 hours.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since we want to mow only the area of the lawn, we can assume that the lawn is evenly divided among the mowing workers. Therefore, we can divide the work required by the number of people:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Number of people needed = Work required / Number of people
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Number of people needed = 5,000 square feet / 5 people
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Number of people needed = 1,000 people
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since we want to mow only the area of the lawn, which is not mentioned in this problem, the answer would be based on the number of workers who can mow one area equally instead.
