[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Yes, I can help you with that. To find the equation of the oblique asymptote of the graph of $\frac{2x^2 + 7x + 10}{2x + 3},$ we can use polynomial long division.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 1: Divide the leading term of the numerator by the leading term of the denominator.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \frac{2x^2}{2x} + \frac{7x}{2x} + \frac{10}{2x} = x + \frac{7}{2} + \frac{5}{x}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 2: Multiply the result of Step 1 by the denominator and subtract from the original polynomial.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
