[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m What is the units digit of the sum $1! + 2! + 3! + 4! + 5! + \cdots + 1000!$?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Consider \[ S = \sum_{k=1}^{1000} k! \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The \(\text{modulus}\) of every term is at least \(1\), so \(S\) is at least \(\phi(1000) = 400\), which permits \(S = k \cdot 1 + r \cdot (1000-k) = (r+1) \cdot k + (1000 - r)\), that is, \(k \in \{0, 1, ..., 500\}\). So, we can make use of the modulo \(9\) and group all numbers in a consecutive interval modulo \(9\), the inclusive endpoint sits at \(999\), gauge the residue, this we have the attribute \(c = S \bmod 9\) and are able to figure out the remainder:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m   S &\bmod{9} &=
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m     (0-0)19+\sum_{i=0}^{9} 7i+10 \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m     &\bmod{9} &\equiv (0-0)19(7+1)+11
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{align}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
