[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Sure, here is a step-by-step solution to simplify the given query: "Find the sum of the infinite series:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[1 + 2 \left(\dfrac{1}{1998}\right) + 3 \left(\dfrac{1}{1998} \right)^2 + 4 \left(\dfrac{1}{1998} \right)^3 + + \cdots\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We can simplify this series by recognizing it as a geometric series. Let's denote S as the sum of the series:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[S = \sum_{n=1}^{\infty} n \left(\dfrac{1}{1998}\right)^{n-1}\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Multiplying the series term-by-term by \(\dfrac{1}{1998}\):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[S = \dfrac{1}{1998} \sum_{n=1}^{\infty} n \left(\dfrac{1}{1998}\right)^{n-1} = \dfrac{1}{1998} \sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \left(\dfrac{1}{1998}\right)^{n-1}\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, we know that the sum of a geometric series1 with the first term \(a = 1\) and common ratio \(r\) is given by the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\text{Sum of }1^{\text{k}}\text{ th geometric series }S_k = \dfrac{1-r^k}{1-r}\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m If we set \(k = 2\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[S = \dfrac{1 - \left(\dfrac{1}{1998}\right)^2}{1 - \dfrac{1}{1998}}\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Simplifying the denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[S = \dfrac{1 - \left(\dfrac{1}{1998}\right)^2}{\dfrac{1998-1}{1998}} = \dfrac{1 - \left(\dfrac{1}{1998}\right)^2}{\left(\dfrac{1997}{1998}\right)} = 1998 \left(1 - \left(\dfrac{1}{1998}\right)^2\right)\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Expanding the square on the left-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[S = 1998 \left(1 - \dfrac{1}{1997^2}\right) = 1998 - \dfrac{1998}{1997^2}\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So the sum of the infinite series is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[1 + 2 \left(\dfrac{1}{1998}\right) + 3 \left(\dfrac{1}{1998} \right)^2 + 4 \left(\dfrac{1}{1998} \right)^3 + \cdots = 1998 - \dfrac{1998}{199
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
