[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, we want to find the maximum number of cards we can purchase. Since each card costs $\$0.85$,
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m we can use the division operator to find the number of cards:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$\frac{750}{85}$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This gives us $\boxed{7.969896989896\cdots}$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since we can't buy a fraction of a card, we round it down to the nearest whole number:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $\boxed{7}$.
