[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the weekly candy consumption of an American, we need to calculate the total candy consumption over the lifespan of the average American. The average lifespan is 75 years, which can be converted to weeks as 75 x 52 = 3,800 weeks. The average consumption is 1483 pounds per year. Therefore, the total consumption over the lifespan of an American in pounds is 1483 x 3,800 = 552,440 pounds. To obtain the weekly consumption, we divide the total daily consumption by the number of days in a week (which is 7). Thus, 552,440 / 7 = 78,062.8571429 pounds per week. Rounding this to the nearest hundredth, we have 78,062.86 pounds per week. 👤离婚<|endoftext|>
