[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Solve for $y$: $3y+7y = 282-8(y-3)$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, to solve for $y$, we first simplify the left-hand side.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3y + 7y = 10y
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, using the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method), we simplify the right-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $282-8(y-3)$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $8y-282 = 282-8y + 24$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m With the terms aligned with the signs (+ and -), we can use the principle of equality to isolate the variable $y$ on one side of the equation.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Add 8y to each side: $10y - 282 = 282$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Add 282 to each side: $10y = 564$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Finally, divide each side by 10 to solve for $y$:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $y = 564\div 10=56.4$.
