[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m For any number $x$, we are told that $x\&=7-x$ and $\&x = x -7$. What is the value of $\&(12\&)$?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the value of \&(12\&), we need to follow the rules given for the prefix operator App and Deprefix.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We know that App(x, y) means $[result + ob(Ob2'(y))]$, where Ob is the operator of the same name.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So, in this case, we have $\&(x, y) = x + y$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m App(x, 2) means $[result + ob(x,2)]$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So, we can evaluate the first equation as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $x + 2 = \&(x, 2)$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Similarly, App(2, x) means $[result + ob(Ob1'(x))]$,
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m which simplifies to
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $7 - x + x = 7$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So, in this case, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m App(2, x) = 7
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m App(x, 2) = $7 + 2 = 9$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m App(3, x) = $x + 9 = 12$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m App(x, 3) = $10$, and so on.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m By applying the same reasoning, we can evaluate the entire chain of App operations.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m App(15, x) = 30, and so on.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, in general, App(x, y) = x + y + 2 * (y - x).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m App(12, 7) = 12 + 7 + 2 * (7 - 12) = 12 + 7 + 2 * (-5) = 12 + 7 - 10 = \boxed{9}.
