[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Compute: $\dfrac{2^{10}-2^8}{2^7-2^6}$. Express your answer in simplest form.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Given the expression:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$\dfrac{2^{10}-2^8}{2^7-2^6}$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First, we can simplify the numerator and the denominator separately.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. Simplify the numerator \(2^{10} - 2^8\):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$2^{10} - 2^8 = 2^8 \cdot 2^2 - 2^8 = 2^8 \cdot (2^2 - 1) = 2^8 \cdot 3$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. Simplify the denominator \(2^{7} - 2^6\):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$2^{7} - 2^6 = 2^6 \cdot 2^1 - 2^6 = 2^6 \cdot (2 \cdot 2^1 - 1) = 2^6 \cdot (2 \cdot 2 - 1) = 2^6 \cdot (4 - 1) = 2^6 \cdot 3$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now we can rewrite the original expression:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$\dfrac{2^{10}-2^8}{2^7-2^6} = \dfrac{2^8 \cdot 3}{2^6 \cdot 3}$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Notice that \(3\) in the numerator and denominator cancels out:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$\dfrac{2^8 \cdot 3}{2^6 \cdot 3} = \dfrac{2^8}{2^6}$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. Simplify the fraction:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$\dfrac{2^8}{2^6} = 2^{8-6} = 2^2 = 4$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So, the final answer is \(4\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m boxed{4}<|endoftext|>
