[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To convert spherical coordinates $(\rho, \theta, \phi) = \left( 4, \frac{5 \pi}{3}, \frac{\pi}{2} \right)$ to rectangular coordinates $(x, y, z)$, we use the following formulas:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $x = \rho \sin \phi \cos \theta$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $y = \rho \sin \phi \sin \theta$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $z = \rho \cos \phi$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Let's plug in the given spherical coordinates for each angle:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $x = 4 \sin \left(\frac{\pi}{2}\right) \cos \left(\frac{5 \pi}{3}\right)$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $x = 4 \cdot 1 \cdot \left(-\frac{1}{2}\right)$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $x = -2$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $y = 4 \sin \left(\frac{\pi}{2}\right) \sin \left(\frac{5 \pi}{3}\right)$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $y = 4 \cdot 1 \cdot \left(-\frac{1}{2}\right)$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $y = -2$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $z = 4 \cos \left(\frac{\pi}{2}\right)$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $z = 4 \cdot 0$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $z = 0$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Putting the values together, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $x = -2$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $y = -2$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $z = 0$
