[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the coordinates of the intersection point \(P\) of the two lines, we set the two equations equal to each other:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -3 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} + t \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 1 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 2 \\ -10 \end{pmatrix} + u \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -1 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This gives us the system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2t + u = -2
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m t - u = 1
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We can solve this system by adding the two equations. First, subtract the second equation from the first:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m (2t + u) - (t - u) = -2 - 1
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m t + 2u = -3
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now we have a single equation in two variables:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m t + 2u = -3
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We can solve for \(t\) in terms of \(u\):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m t = -3 - 2u
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Next, we substitute this expression for \(t\) into the first equation:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2(-3 - 2u) + u = -2
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Simplify and solve for \(u\):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m -6 - 4u + u = -2
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m -6 - 3u = -2
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m -3u = 4
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m u = -\frac{4}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now substitute \(u = -\frac{4}{3}\) back into the expression for \(t\):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m t = -3 - 2\left(-\frac{4}{3}\right)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m t = -3 + \frac{8}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m t = -\frac{9}{3} + \frac{8}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
