[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find out how many megabytes of disk space one hour of music takes up on average, we first need to determine the disk space usage per hour.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We start with the information that one day of music takes up 16,000 megabytes of disk space. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the disk space usage for one hour, we divide the day's disk space (16,000 mb) by the number of hours (12):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \frac{16000 \, \text{mb}}{12 \, \text{hours}} = 1333.33\, \text{mb per hour}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Next, we should express this result to the nearest whole number. We can do that by rounding 1333.33 to the nearest integer. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1333.33 rounded to the nearest integer gives us 1333.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, the average disk space utilization for one hour of music in this digital music library is \(\boxed{1333}\) megabytes.<|endoftext|>
