[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m From $A$ to $B$ along the edges, we start at $A$ and travel three edges, $AB, BA, AEB$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m ** The steps here =**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m **How many different 3-edge paths choose + How many 2-edge paths choose + 0-edge paths choose**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m ----------
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. On $AB$, we have $3$ options for the starting point: half of one of the 3 choices are for the starting point and the other half for the ending point, so that we have $\binom32=3$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. On $BA$, we have $1$ option for the starting point
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. On $AEB$, we have $0$ options for the ending point, however we can leave $AB$ a 2-edge active path, so that we have $2$ options
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 4. On $EBD$, we have $0$ options for the ending point, however we can leave $AB$ a 2-edge active path, so that we have $2$ options
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We have $\binom31\binom20\binom30(2^25)(2^25)2^25)(2^25)\binom20(2^25)$ total paths
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Video_a few more times..:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First internal diagonal from $a_{1,4}$ to $a_{5,1}$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First internal diagonal from $a_{2,3}$ to $a_{4,2}$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m aka Super simple walk on vertices
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m last internal diagonal from $a_{2,3}$ to $a_{5,1}$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We have $5$ ways to pick the direction.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m For each action, we shift the number of steps left (shortcuts to $A$ and $B$)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$ n_{A}=\begin{cases}|a_{i,i}|&i=1,2,3\\|a_{i,i+1}|-|a_{i,i+2}|\end{cases}\qquad(n_{A}>0) $$ $$ n_{B}=\begin{cases}|a_{i,i}|&i=5,4,3\\|a_{i,i-1}|-|a_{i,i+2}|\end{cases}\qquad(n_{B}>0) $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since area is 1, the number of $A$ and $B$ everywhere plus $A$ and $B$ everywhere minus $A$ and $B$ (to go from $A$, $B$) equals 1.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now sneak a peek into ABD
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$ n_{A}+n_{A}n_{B}+n_{B}+n_{A}-n_{A}-n_{B}+\iota $$ $$=\begin{cases}\binom33&5\\(\binom32\binom20\binom20+\binom23\binom30\binom30)&6\\(\binom33)&7\\-&6&8\\3&|\iota|&9\\-\binom31\binom22&10\\5&11\\-\binom31\\1&12\\1\end{cases} $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
