[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Explanation: The `re.findall()` function is used to extract all non-overlapping matches of the pattern given by the main regex expression. In this case, the pattern is `\w+`, which matches one or more word characters. The main regex expression defines a range of characters and their appearances within string, so we use a proper syntax parsing in Python. The `re.findall()` function returns a list of all matches, which we store in the `grouped` list.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
