[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This regular expression contains the following parts:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. The `(?<=kh)"` is a group of characters from "kh", and the parentheses around it are used to restrict search. This is necessary to avoid matching the whole character "kh", which would resemble another character.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. The `"` is a single quote to denote the end of the string.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. The `?""` is part of the string "kh" and asserts that it should be a single character.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, the main regex expression effectively matches any character after the first character "kh" until a single quote, so it should match the word "kh", which is the specific word phrase you were talking about in the question.
