[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To solve the equation \(x^4 + 64 = 0\), we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. **Isolate \(x^4\):**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    x^4 = -64
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. **Find the fourth roots of \(-64\):**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    Any number raised to the fourth power will have the same magnitude as \(-64\), but possibly with a different sign due to the negative sign. Therefore,
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    x^4 = 64 \implies x = \pm 2\sqrt{6}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    and
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    x^4 = -64 \implies x = \pm \sqrt[4]{64} i = \pm 2\sqrt{2} i
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. **Simplify the fourth roots:**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    Note that \(\sqrt[4]{64} = 4\), so the fourth roots of \(64\) are \(2\) and \(-2\) with each having two identical roots \(-2\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    Thus, the solutions are:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    x = \pm 2\sqrt{6}, \quad x = 2\sqrt{6}, \quad x = -2\sqrt{6}, \quad x = -2\sqrt{6}, \quad x = 2\sqrt{6}, \quad x = -2\sqrt{6}, \quad x = 2\sqrt{6}, \quad x = -2\sqrt{6}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 4. **List all unique solutions:**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    We collected five distinct solutions:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    x_1 = \pm 2\sqrt{6}, \quad x_2 = 2\sqrt{6}, \quad x_3 = -2\sqrt{6}, \quad x_4 = -2\sqrt{6}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, the solutions to the equation \(x^4 + 64 = 0\) are:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \boxed{2\sqrt{6}, 2\sqrt{6}, -2\sqrt{6}, -2\sqrt{6}}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
