[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To solve this problem, we need to find the sum of the first $n$ positive even integers. These integers can be represented as $2, 4, 6, \ldots, 2n$. This sequence will have $n-1$ terms.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The total sum of the first $n$ even integers is given by the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ S_n = n^2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Given that the sum of the first $m$ positive odd integers is $212$ more than the sum of the first $n$ positive even integers, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ m^2 - n(n-1) = 212 + n \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This equation needs to be solved for $m$ and $n$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
