[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m In how many ways can George choose two out of seven colors to paint his room?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Yes, I can help you. Here's the detailed explanation:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m George has seven colors to choose from when painting his room. He needs to choose two out of these seven colors.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the number of combinations (ways to choose) George can do this, we can use the formula for permutations, which is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m P(n, r) = n! / (n - r)!
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m In this case, n = 7 (the total number of colors) and r = 2 (the number of colors he needs to choose).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So, we can calculate P(7, 2):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 7! / (7 - 2)! = 7! / 5!
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 7! = 7 × 6 × 5 × 4 × 3 × 2 × 1 = 5040
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 4! = 4 × 3 × 2 × 1 = 24
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So, P(7, 2) = 5040 / 24 = 210
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m George can choose 2 out of 7 colors in 210 different ways.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
