[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the percentage of problems Lacy got correct, we first need to determine how many problems she got right.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - Total problems = \(5x\)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - Problems Lacy missed = \(x\)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - Success rate = \(\frac{\text{number of successful problems}}{\text{total problems}}\)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Using the success rate:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{Number of successful problems} = \text{Total problems} - \text{Number of missed problems}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Substitute the values:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{Number of successful problems} = (5x) - (x) = 4x
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, calculate the percentage of problems Lacy got correct:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{Percentage correct} = \left(\frac{\text{Number of successful problems}}{\text{Total problems}}\right) \times 100
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Substitute the values:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{Percentage correct} = \left(\frac{4x}{5x}\right) \times 100
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Simplify the fraction:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{Percentage correct} = \left(\frac{4}{5}\right) \times 100
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Calculate the result:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{Percentage correct} = 0.8 \times 100 = 80\%
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Thus, the percentage of problems Lacy got correct is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \boxed{80\%}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
