[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m If \[x^3 - 52x^2 + 581x - k\] has roots that are distinct prime numbers, then its polynomial can be written in the following form: \[x^3 - 52x^2 + 581x - k = (x-1)(x-2)(x-r)\]Where $r$ is a prime number.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m If $x=2$, substituting into the equation, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[2^3 - 52(2^2) + 581(2) - k = 0\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Simplifying, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[8 - 52(4) + 581(2) - k = 0\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[- 169 = k\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, the value of $k$ is \[-169\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
