[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Let $f(x) = 2x+1$ and $g(x) = f(2x) - 3$. What is $g(g(2))$?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Yes, I understand it!
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First, let's find $g(2)$ using the definition of $g(x)$:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m g(x)& = f(2x) - 3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m & = f\left( \dfrac{2(x-1)}{x}\right) -3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m & = 2 \left( \dfrac{2(x-1)}{x} \right) +1 -3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m & = \dfrac{4(x-1)}{x} +1 -3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m & = \dfrac{4(x-1)}{x} -2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, we have $g(2) = \dfrac{4(x-1)}{x} -2$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Next, we can find $g(g(2))$ by substituting $g(2)$ into $g(x)$:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m g(g(2)) &= g\left( \dfrac{4(x-1)}{x} -2 \right) \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &= \dfrac{4( \dfrac{4(x-1)}{x} -2-1)}{ \dfrac{4(x-1)}{x} -2} - 2 \\
