[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the minimum value of the quadratic expression $5x^2 - 20x + 1357$, we need to find the vertex of the parabola represented by this equation. A parabola can have a maximum or minimum value, and it is given by the formula for the x-coordinate of the vertex:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m [ x_vertex = frac{{-b} pm sqrt{{b^2} - 4ac}}{2a} ]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Given the quadratic equation:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m [ 5x^2 - 20x + 1357 ]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The coefficients are:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m [ a = 5 ]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m [ b = "-20" ]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m [ c = "1357" ]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First, calculate the discriminant $D$:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m [ D = b^2 - 4ac ]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m [ D = (-20)^2 - 4 * 5 * 1357 = 400 - 27250 = -26850 ]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since the discriminant ($D$) is negative, the parabola opens downwards and has a maximum value at the vertex.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Next, substitute $a$, $b$, and $D$ into the formula to find the x-coordinate of the vertex:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m [ x_vertex = frac{{-b} pm sqrt{{b^2} - 4ac}}{2a} ]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m [ x_vertex = frac{{-(-20) pm sqrt{(-20)^2 - 45 cdot 1357}}{2 cdot 5}]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now we will compute the values:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m [ x_vertex = frac{{20 pm sqrt{400 - 27250}}{10} ]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m [ x_vertex = frac{{20 pm sqrt{400 - 27250}}{10} ]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m [ x_vertex = frac{{20 pm 195.2}}{10} ]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m [ x_vertex = frac{{-175.2}}{10} ]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Finally, compute the corresponding y-coordinate using the vertex formula:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m [ y_vertex = a cdot x_vertex^2 + b cdot x_vertex + c ]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Thus, the minimum quadratic value is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m [ \boxed{c + x_vertex^2} ]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This leads to:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m [ \boxed{1357 + left(frac{{-175.2}}{10}right)^2} ]<|endoftext|>
