[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To solve the equation \(\log_{x-1}(10-2x) = 2\), we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. **Rewrite the logarithmic equation using the definition of logarithms:**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \log_{x-1}(10-2x) = 2
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    This implies:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    x-1 = 10^{2}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. **Simplify the right-hand side:**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    10^{2} = 100
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    So the equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    x-1 = 100
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. **Solve for \(x\):**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    x = 100 + 1
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    x = 101
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Thus, the value of \(x\) that satisfies the equation \(\log_{x-1}(10-2x) = 2\) is \(\boxed{101}\).<|endoftext|>
