[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m In this case, \( n = 50 \) and \( r = 2 \). Plugging these values into the formula, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \binom{50}{2} = \frac{50!}{2!(50-2)!} = \frac{50!}{2! \cdot 48!}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Here’s how the calculation proceeds:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. **Simplify the factorials using properties of factorials:**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 50! &= 1 \times 2 \times 3 \times \ldots \times 50 \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 48! &= 1 \times 2 \times 3 \times \ldots \times 48 \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. **Cancel out the common terms \(48!\) in the numerator and denominator:**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \frac{50!}{2! \cdot 48!} &= \frac{50 \times 49 \times 48!}{2! \times 48!} \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &= \frac{50 \times 49}{2!} \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3. **Compute \(2!\):**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2! = 2 \times 1 = 2
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 4. **Substitute \(2!\) back into the equation:**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \frac{50 \times 49}{2} &= \frac{50 \times 49}{2} \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 5. **Calculate the product in the numerator:**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 50 \times 49 &= 2450
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 6. **Divide the result by 2:**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \frac{2450}{2} = 1225
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, the result of \(\binom{50}{2}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \boxed{1225}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
