[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To solve for $\mathbf{M}$, we'll use the formula $\mathbf{M} \mathbf{A} = \mathbf{I}$ in the matrix equation. Given $\mathbf{A}$: $\begin{pmatrix} -3 & 4 & 0 \\ 5 & -7 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}$, and $\mathbf{I}$: $\mathbf{I} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}$, we know that we want:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\mathbf{M} \mathbf{A} = \mathbf{I}\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This can be rewritten as:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\mathbf{M} \mathbf{A} = \mathbf{I}\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To solve for $\mathbf{M}$, we can write $\mathbf{M}$ as:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\mathbf{M} = \mathbf{I}^{-1} \mathbf{A}\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The inverse of a 3x3 matrix $\mathbf{A}$, denoted $\mathbf{A}^{-1}$, is a matrix $\mathbf{B}$ such that:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B} = \mathbf{B} \mathbf{A} = \mathbf{I}\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since $\mathbf{A}$ is a 3x3 matrix with zeros and 1 in the last column, the inverse of $\mathbf{A}$ will also have zeros in the first 3 columns and 1 in the last column, but the columns in the second column of $\mathbf{A}^{-1}$ will be the same as the columns of $\mathbf{A}$ except they will have the corresponding entries taken out by the multiplicative inverse of the corresponding column of $\mathbf{A}$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So we find:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\mathbf{A} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 & 4 & 0 \\ 5 & -7 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\mathbf{A}^{-1} = \begin{pmatrix} -1 & -4 & 0 \\ 5 & 2 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Then we can calculate $\mathbf{M}$:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\mathbf{I}^{-1} \mathbf{A} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} -3 & 4 & 0 \\ 5 & -7 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 & 4 & 0 \\ 5 & -7 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since we are wanting $\mathbf{M} = \mathbf{I}^{-1} \mathbf{A}$, we can choose the columns of $\mathbf{A}$ to be $\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 5 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ -7 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}$ to get the inverse matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\mathbf{M} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 & 4 \\ 5 & -7 \end{pmatrix}\]
