[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Absolutely, we start by taking advantage of the properties of logarithms:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 10 &\log_4 x + 2 \log_2 x^2 = 10 \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &\Rightarrow 10 \log_4 x + 2 \cdot 2 \log_2 x = 10 \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &\Rightarrow \log_4 x + \log_2 x^2 = \log_4 10 \>}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, using the fact that $\log_4 10 = \log_{10} 10^{\log_4 10} / \log_4 10$ and Snoopy's property of logarithms,
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \log_4 x + \log_2 x^2 &\Leftrightarrow \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \log_4 x + \log_2^{3} x &= \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &\Rightarrow \log_4 x + 3 \log_2 x \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &\Leftrightarrow \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &\Rightarrow \log_{4^2} x + \log_4 x  &&\text{Using Thag' Fun property:} \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &\Rightarrow \frac{\log_4 x + \log_4 x}{\log_4 x} &&\text{Step 1:} \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &\Rightarrow \log_4 x &&\text{Step 2:} \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &\Leftrightarrow \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &\Rightarrow \log_4 x = 2 \log_2 x
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, assuming the three equation $\log_4 x = 2 \log_2 x = \log_4 10$ hold, it follows that \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m x &=10^2\cdot 4 = 4\cdot 10^2 = 1000
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{align*} We check that our assumptions satisfy the original equation by rewriting $\log_4 10 = \log_{10} 10^{\log_4 10} / \log_4 10$ as $\log_{10} 10^{\log_4 10} / \log_4 10=\log_{10} 10^6 / \log_4 10 = 6$ hence our assumption is correct. Hence $x = 1000$.<|endoftext|>
