[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m A curve is described parametrically by
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[(x,y) = (2 \cos t - \sin t, 4 \sin t).\]The graph of the curve can be expressed in the form
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ax^2 + bxy + cy^2 = 1.\]Enter the ordered triple $(a,b,c).$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The parametric equations for the curve are:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \((x, y) = (2 \cos t - \sin t, 4 \sin t)\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Expanding the terms:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[x = 2 (\cos t \cos t - \sin t \sin t),\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[y = 4 (\sin t \cos t).\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Simplifying:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[x = 2 (\cos^2 t - \sin^2 t),\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[y = 4 \sin t \cos t.\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Rearranging terms:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[x = 2 \cos 2t,\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[y = 2 \cos t \sin t.\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This is now in the form Ax^2 + Bxy + Cy^2 = 1. Thus,
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\boxed{a = 2,\; b = 0,\; c = 2}.\]<|endoftext|>
