[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m If $x \ge 0$ and $y \ge 0$, then
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[|x + y + z| + |x + y - z| = \sqrt{(x + y)^2 + z^2} + \sqrt{(x + y)^2 + z^2} = 2\sqrt{(x + y)^2 + z^2}.\]Since $x^2 + y^2 \ge 0$ and $z^2 \ge 0,$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[2\sqrt{x^2 + y^2 + z^2}\ge 2\sqrt{z^2} \implies \sqrt{(x + y)^2 + z^2} \ge |z|.\] Thus,
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[2\sqrt{(x + y)^2 + z^2} \ge 2|x + y| + z,\]which means that
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[z \le |x + y| + 4.\]By Cauchy-Schwarz,
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[|x + y| \cdot |x + y| \ge 2(\sqrt{x^2 + y^2} + \sqrt{z^2} + z) = 2\sqrt{x^2 + y^2 + z^2} + 2z + \hfill\\ = \sqrt{(x + y)^2 + z^2} + 2\sqrt{x^2 + y^2 + z^2} + z.\]Thus,
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[z \le |x + y| + 2\sqrt{x^2 + y^2 + z^2} + \sqrt{(x + y)^2 + z^2}.\]Since
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[|x + y| + 2\sqrt{x^2 + y^2 + z^2} + \sqrt{(x + y)^2 + z^2} \le 8,\]$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m we can say that the region is contained in the triangle determined by the points $\{ (0, 0, 0), (2, 0, 0), (2, 2, 0)\}$ and
