[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Find the volume of the region in space defined by
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[|x + y + z| + |x + y - z| \le 8\]and $x,$ $y,$ $z \ge 0.$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We first want to consider the region defined by
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[|x + y + z| + |x + y - z| \le 8.\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Because $x,$ $y,$ and $z \ge 0,$ we can rewrite this inequality as
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[2\sqrt{2}(|x + y|+|z|) \le 8.\]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Note each expression inside the parentheses is non-negative. There are four cases to consider:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Case 1: $\sqrt{2}|-x - y| \le \sqrt{2}$ and $\sqrt{2}|\sqrt{2}z| \le \sqrt{2}$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Case 2: $\sqrt{2}|-x - y| \le \sqrt{2}$ and $0 < \sqrt{2}z \le \sqrt{2}$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Case 3: $-\sqrt{2}|-x - y| \le \sqrt{2}$ and $\sqrt{2}|\sqrt{2}z| \le \sqrt{2}$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Case 4: $-\sqrt{2}|-x - y| \le \sqrt{2}$ and $0 < \sqrt{2}z \le \sqrt{2}$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m In Case 1 and Case 2, $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ are all non-negative, so their absolute values make sense. Furthermore, in Case 1, the absolute value of $x + y$ is minimized when $x = y = 0$ and $z = \sqrt{2}$, so the area of this region is $\sqrt{2}$. In Case 2, $z$ is unrestricted, so the area of this region is $2\sqrt{2}$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m In Case 3 and Case 4, for each $x,$ $y,$ and $z$, exactly one of $x + y$ or $z$ is nonnegative, so the volume of this region is bounded by $0$. This is why the volume is bounded by 4 possible values, one for each $x,$ $y,$ and $z$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, the total volume of the region is
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\boxed{\sqrt{2} + 2\sqrt{2} + 4\sqrt{2}}.\]
