[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m It appears that the initial approach missed the fact that \(y - 1 > 1\) and \(x - 1 > 1\). These constraints will give us the second favorable condition of the inequality \(f(x, y) = \frac{x^2}{y-1} + \frac{y^2}{x-1}\) to be greater than or equal to 4. Therefore, the first favorable condition given by AM-GM inequality becomes:
