[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Find the modulo 4 residue of $17 \cdot 18$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 18 &\equiv 2 \pmod 4\\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 17 &\equiv 3 \pmod 4
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m (17 \cdot 18) \pmod 4 &= (17 \cdot 18) \pmod 4
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 17 \pmod 4 &\equiv 1 \pmod 4\\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 18 \pmod 4 &\equiv 2 \pmod 4
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m therefore we obtain $(17 \cdot 18) \pmod 4 \equiv (3 \cdot 2)\pmod 4 \equiv \boxed{2}\pmod 4$.
