[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To solve the problem, we need to consider two cases: one where the president and the vice-president are of the same gender, and one where they are of different genders.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. If the president and the vice-president are of the same gender, we have 10 decisions for the president (since there are 10 boys) and 10 decisions for the vice-president (since there are 10 girls). Therefore, the total number of ways is \( 10 \times 10 = 100 \).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. If the president and the vice-president are of different genders, then we have 10 boys and 10 girls. We can choose the president of either gender in 10 ways, and then choose a girl out of the girls in 10 ways. Similarly, we can choose a boy out of the boys in 10 ways. Therefore, the total number of ways is \( 10 \times 10 \times 10 \times 10 = 10^{2} = 100 \).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The total number of ways to choose the president and vice-president is the sum of the two cases, which is \( 100 + 100 = 200 \).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So, the answer is \( \boxed{200} \).<|endoftext|>
