[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To solve this problem, we need to distribute the balloons equally among Winnie's 8 friends while ensuring each friend receives an equal number of balloons. We'll do this by first finding the total number of balloons and then dividing it to find the number of balloons each friend will receive.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 1: Calculate the total number of balloons
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Winnie has 17 red, 33 white, 65 green, and 83 chartreuse balloons. Adding these together:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ 17 + 33 + 65 + 83 = 198 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 2: Divide the total number of balloons by the number of friends
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Winnie has 8 friends, so we need to divide the total number of balloons by 8:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ 198 \div 8 = 24 \text{ remainder } 6 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This means each friend will receive 24 balloons, and there will be 6 balloons left over. Since Winnie won't be distributing these 6 balloons, she will keep all of them as her final count.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, Winnie ends up keeping \(\boxed{24}\) balloons.<|endoftext|>
