[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Yes, that is correct. Rewriting $6y^2 - y - 51 = (3Ay + B)(y - C)$ will give us $B = -C$ and $8C^2 - 1$ is positive. So $\boxed{{BC}^2 - 8C^2 = 9}$, so $\boxed{{BC}^2 = 9 + 8C^2}$ and thus $AC^2 = (9 + 8C^2)^2 - 8C^4 = AC^2 - 8C^4 = (AC)^2 - 2^2(4C^2)^2 = (AC)^2 - 8C^4 = (AC)^2 - 2^6$, so $(AC)^2 - 8C^4 = 1$ and $\boxed{{AC}^2 - 8C^4 = 1 + 8(-2^2)} = -16$.
