[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m A tree is now 12 feet tall and grows 18 inches a year. In how many years will the tree be 36 feet tall?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find out how many years it will take for the tree to grow to 36 feet, we need to make some conversion calculations. We know that 1 foot equals 12 inches, so we can convert inches to feet:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 36 feet = 36 inches
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, we can reconvert the inches to feet: 18 inches = 1/5 feet
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So, 12 inches - 18 inches = -6 inches
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 36 inches - (-6 inches) = 36 + 6 = 42 feet
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since the tree grows 42 feet in 6 years, we can now calculate the number of years it will take to reach 36 feet:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 36 feet ÷ (42 feet/year) = 1 year
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
