[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Joann ate a total of 100 lollipops in five days. Each day after the first day she ate six more than she had eaten on the previous day. How many lollipops did she eat on the third day?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m NO controvence.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We know that on the first day Joann ate 6 lollipops, so on the second day she ate 6 + 6 = 12 lollipops.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m On the third day, she ate 12 + 6 = 18 lollipops.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m On the fourth day, she ate 18 + 6 = 24 lollipops.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m On the fifth day, she ate 24 + 6 = 30 lollipops.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, Joann ate 30 lollipops on the third day.
