[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m A line is parameterized by
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} + t \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix}.\]A second line is parameterized by
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[\begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix} + u \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 4 \end{pmatrix}.\]Find the point where the lines intersect.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Let's find the intersection points of the two lines. A intersection point can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m x=\frac{2-3t}{-1+t}\\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m y=3+5t
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \text{ and
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m }
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m x=0-utt\\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m y=7-(4u-1)t
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We can solve these two set of equations. First, solve the first equation for $x$:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \frac{2-3t}{-1+t}=\frac{2}{3t}-3
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This gives us
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2\left(3t-1\right)=-3t+6t^2
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m which simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 6t^2-3t-6=0 \tag {1}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We can factor the quadratic equation as:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 3t-2=\frac{3}{2}\tag{2}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Next, solve this quadratic. We see that $t=2$. Substitute this back into equation (1) for $x$:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 6(2)^2-3(2)-6=0 \tag {3}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This is consistent to both (1) and (2). The forum = gets a point at $\boxed{(5,5)}$. UIAlertActionsystem
