[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To determine \(\sin{X}\) in the right triangle \(XYZ\), where \(X\) is the angle opposite the leg of length 10, \(Y\) is the angle opposite the leg of length 8, and \(Z\) is the angle opposite the hypotenuse of length 10, we can use the definitions and properties of trigonometric functions in right triangles.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 1: Identify the sine of an angle in a right triangle
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The sine of an angle \(\angle Y\) (opposite side 8) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \sin{Y} = \frac{\text{opposite}}{\text{hypotenuse}} = \frac{8}{10} = \frac{4}{5}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 2: Verify the angle
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We know that the sum of angles in a triangle is \(180^\circ\). Therefore,:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \angle X + \angle Y + \angle Z = 180^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since \(\angle Y = 90^\circ\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \angle X + 90^\circ + \angle Z = 180^\circ \implies \angle X + \angle Z = 90^\circ
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This confirms that \(\angle X\) is indeed the complementary angle to \(90^\circ\) when \(\angle Y = 90^\circ\). Therefore, we can directly use the trigonometric identity for \(\sin\):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \sin{X} = \sqrt{1 - \cos^2{X}}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since \(X = 45^\circ\) (because we know \(\angle X\) is supplementary to \(90^\circ\) since it is in a right triangle), we can use the fact that \(\sin{45^\circ} = \cos{45^\circ} = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}\). Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \sin{X} = \cos{45^\circ} = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Answer<|endoftext|>
