[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m If the six solutions of $x^6=-64$ are written in the form $a+bi$, where $a$ and $b$ are real, find the product of those solutions with $a>0.$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the six solutions of the equation \(x^6 = -64\), we start by expressing \(-64\) in polar form. The number \(-64\) can be written as \(64 \text{cis} (180^\circ)\) or \(64 e^{i(180^\circ)}\). The general form for the \(n\)-th roots of a complex number \(r \text{cis} \theta\) is given by \(r^{1/n} e^{i(\theta + 360^\circ k/n)}\) for \(k = 0, 1, \ldots, n-1\). In our case, \(r = 64\), \(\theta = 180^\circ\), and \(n = 6\). Thus, the roots are:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &x_1 = 64^{1/6} e^{i \cdot 180^\circ} = 2 e^{i \cdot 30^\circ} = 2 \left( -\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} + i \frac{1}{2} \right) = -\sqrt{3} + i \frac{1}{2}, \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &x_2 = 64^{1/6} e^{i \cdot 30^\circ} = -\sqrt{3} - i \frac{1}{2}, \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &x_3 = -\sqrt{3464} e^{i \cdot 30^\circ} = -8 e^{i \cdot 30^\circ} = -8 \left( \cos 30^\circ + i \sin 30^\circ \right) = -8 \left( \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} + i \frac{1}{2} \right) = -4\sqrt{3} + 4i, \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &x_4 = -8 \cdot e^{i \cdot 30^\circ} = -8 \left( \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} + i \frac{1}{2} \right) = -4\sqrt{3} - \frac{1}{2}i, \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &x_5 = -8 \cdot e^{i \cdot 30^\circ} = -8 \left( \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} + i \frac{1}{2} \right) = -4\sqrt{3} + \frac{1}{2}i, \\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &x_6 = -8 \cdot e^{i \cdot 30^\circ} = -8 \left( \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} + i \frac{1}{2} \right) = -4\sqrt{3} - i \frac{1}{2}.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Among these complex numbers, the ones with \(a > 0\) are \(-4\sqrt{3} + i \frac{1}{2}\) and \(-4\sqrt{3} - i \frac{1}{2}\). The product of these two roots is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m (-4\sqrt{3} + i \frac{1}{2})(-4\sqrt{3} - i \frac{1}{2}) = (-4\sqrt{3})^2 - \left(i \frac{1}{2}\right)^2 = 48 + \frac{1}{4} = \frac{193}{4}.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Thus, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \boxed{\frac{193}{4}}.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
