[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m What is left when $\frac{1}{8}$ is subtracted from $\frac{3}{4}$?
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 1: Identify the fraction. In this case, it is $\frac{7}{24}$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 2: Subtract $\frac{1}{8}$ from $\frac{7}{24}$.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Step 3: 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \frac{7}{24} - \frac{1}{8}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &= \frac{7}{24} - \frac{3}{24}\\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &= \frac{7 - 3}{24}\\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &= \frac{4}{24}\\
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m &= \frac{1}{6}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m So, the final answer is $\boxed{\frac{1}{6}}$.
