[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To compute the projection of vector $\bold{v}$ onto vector $\bold{w}$, we can use the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$\text{proj}_{\bold{w}} \bold{v} = \frac{\bold{v} \cdot \bold{w}}{\bold{w} \cdot \bold{w}} \bold{w}$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m where $\cdot$ denotes the dot product.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First, we need to compute the dot product of $\bold{v}$ and $\bold{w}$:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$\bold{v} \cdot \bold{w} = 0 \cdot 2 + (-4) \cdot 2 + 1 \cdot (-1) = -9$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Next, compute the dot product of $\bold{w}$ with itself:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$\bold{w} \cdot \bold{w} = 2^2 + 2^2 + (-1)^2 = 9$$
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m $$\text{proj}_{\bold{w}} \bold{v} = \frac{-9}{9} \bold{w} = -1 \bold{w} = -1 \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 2 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} = \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ -2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}}$$<|endoftext|>
