[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the possible degrees of the remainder when a polynomial \( p(x) \) is divided by \( -3x^5 + 10x - 11 \), we can use the polynomial division lemma. According to this lemma, if we have a polynomial \( p(x) \) that is exactly divisible by a polynomial \( D(x) \) (dividing \( p(x) \) by \( D(x) \) gives \( p(x) = D(x) \cdot q(x) \)), then the degree of the dividend \( p(x) \) must be a divisor of the degree of the divisor \( D(x) \).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m In this problem, the divisor polynomial is \( -3x^5 + 10x - 11 \). This polynomial is of degree 5. For the division to be exact, the dividend polynomial \( p(x) \) must also be of degree 5. If the degree of the dividend polynomial were any higher, then there would not be an exact remainder when divided by the divisor. Therefore, the possible degree of the remainder when \( p(x) \) is divided by \( -3x^5 + 10x - 11 \) is 5. Here is the reasoning with our solutions:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The possible degrees of the remainder are all those that divide the degree of the divisor polynomial. The degree of the divisor \( -3x^5 + 10x - 11 \) is 5, which means its possible degrees are divisors of 5. The divisors of 5 are 1, 5, and so on. The largest possible divisor of 5 is 5 itself.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Therefore, the possible degrees of the remainder are 1, 5.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m boxed{1,5}
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m ∴ possible values: 1,5<|endoftext|>
