[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m This table organization of notations was provided to me by Monument, and it is one of the best ways to understand logical operators, which are represented by symbols (e.g., X, Y, N, Z, V, T, F, R, I, J). These symbols have over 10,000 blooms.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m I have compiled the following operators description from educational textbooks that are used all over the world:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - OR (<<) operator yields:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Rs = (a or b) ∧ ( a and b )
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Rs = (a or b) ∨ ( a and b )
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - AND (>>) operator yields:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Rs = (a and b) ∨ ( a or b )
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - NOT (¬) operator yields:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Rs = (not a) || ( not b )
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - Exclusive NOT (¬<) operator yields:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Rs = (not a) ∧ (not b)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - Venn diagram representation (1, 2, 3): x
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - Union (U) operator yields:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Rs = a ∪ b
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - Subset (X < X) operator yields:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Rs = any a ∈ X and any b ∈ X
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - And (AN) operator yields:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Rs = (a or b) ∧ (a and b)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - Exclusive AND (AJ) operator yields:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    - Rs = (a and b) ∨ ( a or b )
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - Zero expression or expression itself: 0
