[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Yes, I can help you understand these logical operators. Let's break it down step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The NOT operator (`NOT`) symbolizes the logical NOT (negation) operation. It can be represented by the symbol `¬`. Therefore, for example:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - `¬(not x)` simplifies to x because the negation symbol negates the argument.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Similar notation for the AND operator (`AND`) is `∧`: `(a ∧ b)` means the terms `a` and `b` are both true.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The exclusive NOT operator (`〈`) symbolizes the logical exclusive OR (exclusive or) operation. Given:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - `│``(a ∧ ¬b)` simplifies to `not not a or not b`
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - `¬(│a) <->user(a <->c eg): not a`
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m   - Half expression (`a ∧ ¬b`) simplifies to true because `a ∧ b` produces true. Thus, not `(a ∧ ¬b)` simplifies to false, as `not false`.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m     ````[Code}``
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m     @
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m   - Half expression (`│a`) simplifies to all widgets
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m     - Output: all bottons
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m   - Half expression (`¬(..) <-> widget(flag))`) simplifies to `all widgets`. We can look at the formatted output for easier bracketing.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m     
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m   So, `(op)/~~([...])` means all bottons whose arguments do not match (`not (Op * Arguments)`) or aren't `unsupported(structure)` (`(Op & arg)`).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - And (`∧` or `∨`) is composed of the logical AND operator `(and = f, g = false false)` and the `and = any a, any b any c = cleared` variable. And to extract the first field, write it as: `(a and f) ∧ (b and g)`
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - Exclusive AND (`^` symbol) is an exclusive OR (exclusive or) operation. Same as EXT-TILLE_WORD_TREE_TO_ALL
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - Zero (`0`) represents either the empty set (false) or a boolean one (true). Read more about the rules on [MSDN](https://msdn.microsoft.com/zh-cn/library/Efy1h7bd).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - If any offered term is `false`, `false` is implicitly adopted as true and vice versa.
