[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the number of positive two-digit integers that are multiples of both 5 and 7, we first need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of 5 and 7.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m LCM(5,7) = 35
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, we need to find all the positive two-digit integers that are multiples of 35. 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m The smallest two-digit integer is 10, and the largest is 99. The sequence of multiples of 35 is 35, 70, 105, 140, 175, 210, 245, 280, 315, 350, 385.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Counting the numbers in this sequence, we have 10 integers. So, the final answer is 10.
