[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Thus, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m ax + by +  cz = 1558z
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Since this must hold for all values of \(a\), \(b\), \(c\), \(x\), \(y\), and \(z\), it implies the coefficients of \(x\), \(y\), and \(z\) must add up to the same value. Specifically, \(a\) must divide \(1558z\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Next, we use the condition \(x \neq 0\) to find the relationship between \(a\), \(b\), \(c\), and \(z\). Substituting \(x = \frac{84z}{13 - a}\) into the second equation:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 84z = 23 \left(\frac{84z}{13 - a}\right) + cz
