[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m V = πr²h
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m where V is the volume, r is the radius, and h is the height.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Given that the original height is 2 inches, we can write the new height as 2 + 6 = 8 inches.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We also know that the new volume is the same as the original volume, V = πr²h.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We can substitute the new height into the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m (8)(πr²) = (2)(πr²)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now, we can simplify and solve for r:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m (8) = 2
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Thus, the original radius r is:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \boxed{2 inches}<|endoftext|>
