[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To determine the base-4 representation of the decimal number \(11011000_2\), we first need to understand the relationship between binary and base-4 numbers. A binary number can be converted to a decimal number (base-10) by taking each digit (in this case, the binary digit).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. **Convert binary to decimal:**
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m    11011000_2 = 1 \cdot 2^7 + 1 \cdot 2^6 + 0 \cdot 2^5 + 1 \cdot 2^4 + 1 \cdot 2^3 + 1 \cdot 2^2 + 0 \cdot 2^1 + 0 \cdot 2^0
