[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ -(A - 10) + Br^2 + 50 = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ -A + 10 + Br^2 + 50 = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ Br^2 + 50 + A - 10 = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ Br^2 + A + 40 = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m From the second equation, we can assume \( r \) is the common root:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ r^3 + Br^2 + 50 = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now we have two expressions for \( r^3 \) in terms of \( B \):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 1. \( r^3 = -(A - 10) \)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 2. \( r^3 + Br^2 + 50 = 0 \)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Equating these two expressions:
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ -(A - 10) + Br^2 + 50 = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ -A + 10 + Br^2 + 50 = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ Br^2 + A + 60 = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m From this, we can solve for \( B \):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ B = \frac{-10 - A}{r^2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Now substitute \( B \) back into the first equation to find \( r \):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ r^3 = -(A - 10) \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ r^3 = -(A - 10) + Br^2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m \[ r^3 + Br^2 = A - 10 \]
