[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m To find the value of \(\frac{1}{a} + \frac{1}{b} + \frac{1}{c}\) where \(a, b,\) and \(c\) are the roots of the polynomial \(x^3 + 2x^2 + 5x + 7 = 0\), we can use Vieta's formulas and properties of symmetric sums of roots.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m First, recall Vieta's formulas for a cubic polynomial \(x^3 + px^2 + qx + r = 0\):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - The sum of the roots taken one at a time is \(-p\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - The sum of the roots taken two at a time is \(q\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - The product of the roots is \(-r\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m For the polynomial \(x^3 + 2x^2 + 5x + 7 = 0\):
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - The sum of all roots \(a + b + c = -\frac{p}{1} = -2\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - The sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time \(ab + bc + ca = \frac{q}{1} = 5\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m - The product of the roots \(abc = -\frac{r}{1} = -7\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m We need to find \(\frac{1}{a} + \frac{1}{b} + \frac{1}{c} = \frac{ab + bc + ca}{abc} = \frac{5}{-7} = -\frac{5}{7}\).
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m Let's confirm this with Python code.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m # Since we know the values from Vieta's formulas, we can directly compute the result.
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m p = -sum_of_roots
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m q = sum_of_products_of_roots_two_at_a_time
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m r = -sum_of_roots * *sum_of_roots  # This represents the product of the roots abc
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m # Calculate the sum of reciprocals
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m sum_of_reciprocals = q / a * *q / b * *q / c
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m print(sum_of_reciprocals)
[36m(main_task pid=645570)[0m ```
